{"task_id": "Mbpp/952", "original_task_id": 952, "entry_point": "nCr_mod_p", "prompt": "Write a function to compute the value of ncr mod p.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef nCr_mod_p(n, r, p):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to compute the value of ncr mod p.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def nCr_mod_p(n, r, p): \r\n\tif (r > n- r): \r\n\t\tr = n - r \r\n\tC = [0 for i in range(r + 1)] \r\n\tC[0] = 1 \r\n\tfor i in range(1, n + 1): \r\n\t\tfor j in range(min(i, r), 0, -1): \r\n\t\t\tC[j] = (C[j] + C[j-1]) % p \r\n\treturn C[r] ", "tests": "assert nCr_mod_p(10, 2, 13) == 6\nassert nCr_mod_p(11, 3, 14) == 11\nassert nCr_mod_p(18, 14, 19) == 1", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "calibration", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/930", "original_task_id": 930, "entry_point": "text_match", "prompt": "Write a function that matches a string that has an a followed by zero or more b's by using regex.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef text_match(text):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function that matches a string that has an a followed by zero or more b's by using regex.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import re\r\ndef text_match(text):\r\n        patterns = 'ab*?'\r\n        if re.search(patterns,  text):\r\n                return ('Found a match!')\r\n        else:\r\n                return ('Not matched!')", "tests": "assert text_match(\"msb\") == 'Not matched!'\nassert text_match(\"a0c\") == 'Found a match!'\nassert text_match(\"abbc\") == 'Found a match!'", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "calibration", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/963", "original_task_id": 963, "entry_point": "discriminant_value", "prompt": "Write a function to calculate the discriminant value.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef discriminant_value(x, y, z):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to calculate the discriminant value.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def discriminant_value(x,y,z):\r\n    discriminant = (y**2) - (4*x*z)\r\n    if discriminant > 0:\r\n        return (\"Two solutions\",discriminant)\r\n    elif discriminant == 0:\r\n        return (\"one solution\",discriminant)\r\n    elif discriminant < 0:\r\n        return (\"no real solution\",discriminant)", "tests": "assert discriminant_value(4,8,2)==(\"Two solutions\",32)\nassert discriminant_value(5,7,9)==(\"no real solution\",-131)\nassert discriminant_value(0,0,9)==(\"one solution\",0)", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "calibration", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/870", "original_task_id": 870, "entry_point": "sum_positivenum", "prompt": "Write a function to calculate the sum of the positive numbers of a given list of numbers using lambda function.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef sum_positivenum(nums):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to calculate the sum of the positive numbers of a given list of numbers using lambda function.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def sum_positivenum(nums):\r\n  sum_positivenum = list(filter(lambda nums:nums>0,nums))\r\n  return sum(sum_positivenum)", "tests": "assert sum_positivenum([2, 4, -6, -9, 11, -12, 14, -5, 17])==48\nassert sum_positivenum([10,15,-14,13,-18,12,-20])==50\nassert sum_positivenum([19, -65, 57, 39, 152,-639, 121, 44, 90, -190])==522", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "calibration", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/801", "original_task_id": 801, "entry_point": "test_three_equal", "prompt": "Write a python function to count the number of equal numbers from three given integers.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef test_three_equal(x, y, z):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to count the number of equal numbers from three given integers.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def test_three_equal(x,y,z):\r\n  result= set([x,y,z])\r\n  if len(result)==3:\r\n    return 0\r\n  else:\r\n    return (4-len(result))", "tests": "assert test_three_equal(1,1,1) == 3\nassert test_three_equal(-1,-2,-3) == 0\nassert test_three_equal(1,2,2) == 2", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "calibration", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/964", "original_task_id": 964, "entry_point": "word_len", "prompt": "Write a python function to check whether the length of the word is even or not.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef word_len(s):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to check whether the length of the word is even or not.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def word_len(s): \r\n    s = s.split(' ')   \r\n    for word in s:    \r\n        if len(word)%2==0: \r\n            return True  \r\n        else:\r\n          return False", "tests": "assert word_len(\"program\") == False\nassert word_len(\"solution\") == True\nassert word_len(\"data\") == True", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "calibration", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/947", "original_task_id": 947, "entry_point": "len_log", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the length of the shortest word.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef len_log(list1):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the length of the shortest word.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def len_log(list1):\r\n    min=len(list1[0])\r\n    for i in list1:\r\n        if len(i)<min:\r\n            min=len(i)\r\n    return min", "tests": "assert len_log([\"win\",\"lose\",\"great\"]) == 3\nassert len_log([\"a\",\"ab\",\"abc\"]) == 1\nassert len_log([\"12\",\"12\",\"1234\"]) == 2", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "calibration", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/772", "original_task_id": 772, "entry_point": "remove_length", "prompt": "Write a function to remove all the words with k length in the given string.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef remove_length(test_str, K):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to remove all the words with k length in the given string.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def remove_length(test_str, K):\r\n  temp = test_str.split()\r\n  res = [ele for ele in temp if len(ele) != K]\r\n  res = ' '.join(res)\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert remove_length('The person is most value tet', 3) == 'person is most value'\nassert remove_length('If you told me about this ok', 4) == 'If you me about ok'\nassert remove_length('Forces of darkeness is come into the play', 4) == 'Forces of darkeness is the'", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "calibration", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/655", "original_task_id": 655, "entry_point": "fifth_Power_Sum", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the sum of fifth power of n natural numbers.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef fifth_Power_Sum(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the sum of fifth power of n natural numbers.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def fifth_Power_Sum(n) : \r\n    sm = 0 \r\n    for i in range(1,n+1) : \r\n        sm = sm + (i*i*i*i*i) \r\n    return sm ", "tests": "assert fifth_Power_Sum(2) == 33\nassert fifth_Power_Sum(4) == 1300\nassert fifth_Power_Sum(3) == 276", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "calibration", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/907", "original_task_id": 907, "entry_point": "lucky_num", "prompt": "Write a function to print the first n lucky numbers.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef lucky_num(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to print the first n lucky numbers.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def lucky_num(n):\r\n List=range(-1,n*n+9,2)\r\n i=2\r\n while List[i:]:List=sorted(set(List)-set(List[List[i]::List[i]]));i+=1\r\n return List[1:n+1]", "tests": "assert lucky_num(10)==[1, 3, 7, 9, 13, 15, 21, 25, 31, 33] \nassert lucky_num(5)==[1, 3, 7, 9, 13]\nassert lucky_num(8)==[1, 3, 7, 9, 13, 15, 21, 25]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "calibration", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/733", "original_task_id": 733, "entry_point": "find_first_occurrence", "prompt": "Write a function to find the index of the first occurrence of a given number in a sorted array.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef find_first_occurrence(A, x):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the index of the first occurrence of a given number in a sorted array.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def find_first_occurrence(A, x):\r\n    (left, right) = (0, len(A) - 1)\r\n    result = -1\r\n    while left <= right:\r\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\r\n        if x == A[mid]:\r\n            result = mid\r\n            right = mid - 1\r\n        elif x < A[mid]:\r\n            right = mid - 1\r\n        else:\r\n            left = mid + 1\r\n    return result", "tests": "assert find_first_occurrence([2, 5, 5, 5, 6, 6, 8, 9, 9, 9], 5) == 1\nassert find_first_occurrence([2, 3, 5, 5, 6, 6, 8, 9, 9, 9], 5) == 2\nassert find_first_occurrence([2, 4, 1, 5, 6, 6, 8, 9, 9, 9], 6) == 4", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "calibration", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/865", "original_task_id": 865, "entry_point": "ntimes_list", "prompt": "Write a function to print n-times a list using map function.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef ntimes_list(nums, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to print n-times a list using map function.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def ntimes_list(nums,n):\r\n    result = map(lambda x:n*x, nums) \r\n    return list(result)", "tests": "assert ntimes_list([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7],3)==[3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18, 21]\nassert ntimes_list([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7],4)==[4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28]\nassert ntimes_list([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7],10)==[10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "calibration", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
