{"task_id": "Mbpp/888", "original_task_id": 888, "entry_point": "substract_elements", "prompt": "Write a function to substract the elements of the given nested tuples.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef substract_elements(test_tup1, test_tup2):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to substract the elements of the given nested tuples.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def substract_elements(test_tup1, test_tup2):\r\n  res = tuple(tuple(a - b for a, b in zip(tup1, tup2))\r\n   for tup1, tup2 in zip(test_tup1, test_tup2))\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert substract_elements(((1, 3), (4, 5), (2, 9), (1, 10)), ((6, 7), (3, 9), (1, 1), (7, 3))) == ((-5, -4), (1, -4), (1, 8), (-6, 7))\nassert substract_elements(((13, 4), (14, 6), (13, 10), (12, 11)), ((19, 8), (14, 10), (12, 2), (18, 4))) == ((-6, -4), (0, -4), (1, 8), (-6, 7))\nassert substract_elements(((19, 5), (18, 7), (19, 11), (17, 12)), ((12, 9), (17, 11), (13, 3), (19, 5))) == ((7, -4), (1, -4), (6, 8), (-2, 7))", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "calibration", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/676", "original_task_id": 676, "entry_point": "remove_extra_char", "prompt": "Write a function to remove everything except alphanumeric characters from the given string by using regex.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef remove_extra_char(text1):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to remove everything except alphanumeric characters from the given string by using regex.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import re\r\ndef remove_extra_char(text1):\r\n  pattern = re.compile('[\\W_]+')\r\n  return (pattern.sub('', text1))", "tests": "assert remove_extra_char('**//Google Android// - 12. ') == 'GoogleAndroid12'\nassert remove_extra_char('****//Google Flutter//*** - 36. ') == 'GoogleFlutter36'\nassert remove_extra_char('**//Google Firebase// - 478. ') == 'GoogleFirebase478'", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "calibration", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/944", "original_task_id": 944, "entry_point": "num_position", "prompt": "Write a function to separate and print the numbers and their position of a given string.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef num_position(text):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to separate and print the numbers and their position of a given string.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import re\r\ndef num_position(text):\r\n for m in re.finditer(\"\\d+\", text):\r\n    return m.start()", "tests": "assert num_position(\"there are 70 flats in this apartment\")==10\nassert num_position(\"every adult have 32 teeth\")==17\nassert num_position(\"isha has 79 chocolates in her bag\")==9", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "calibration", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
