{"task_id": "Mbpp/54", "original_task_id": 54, "entry_point": "counting_sort", "prompt": "Write a function to sort the given array by using counting sort.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef counting_sort(my_list):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to sort the given array by using counting sort.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def counting_sort(my_list):\r\n    max_value = 0\r\n    for i in range(len(my_list)):\r\n        if my_list[i] > max_value:\r\n            max_value = my_list[i]\r\n    buckets = [0] * (max_value + 1)\r\n    for i in my_list:\r\n        buckets[i] += 1\r\n    i = 0\r\n    for j in range(max_value + 1):\r\n         for a in range(buckets[j]):\r\n             my_list[i] = j\r\n             i += 1\r\n    return my_list", "tests": "assert counting_sort([1,23,4,5,6,7,8]) == [1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 23]\nassert counting_sort([12, 9, 28, 33, 69, 45]) == [9, 12, 28, 33, 45, 69]\nassert counting_sort([8, 4, 14, 3, 2, 1]) == [1, 2, 3, 4, 8, 14]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
