{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "original_task_id": 56, "entry_point": "check", "prompt": "Write a python function to check if a given number is one less than twice its reverse.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef check(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to check if a given number is one less than twice its reverse.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def rev(num):    \r\n    rev_num = 0\r\n    while (num > 0):  \r\n        rev_num = (rev_num * 10 + num % 10) \r\n        num = num // 10  \r\n    return rev_num  \r\ndef check(n):    \r\n    return (2 * rev(n) == n + 1)  ", "tests": "assert check(70) == False\nassert check(23) == False\nassert check(73) == True", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
