{"task_id": "Mbpp/60", "original_task_id": 60, "entry_point": "max_len_sub", "prompt": "Write a function to find the maximum length of the subsequence with difference between adjacent elements for the given array.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef max_len_sub(arr, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the maximum length of the subsequence with difference between adjacent elements for the given array.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def max_len_sub( arr, n): \r\n\tmls=[] \r\n\tmax = 0\r\n\tfor i in range(n): \r\n\t\tmls.append(1) \r\n\tfor i in range(n): \r\n\t\tfor j in range(i): \r\n\t\t\tif (abs(arr[i] - arr[j]) <= 1 and mls[i] < mls[j] + 1): \r\n\t\t\t\tmls[i] = mls[j] + 1\r\n\tfor i in range(n): \r\n\t\tif (max < mls[i]): \r\n\t\t\tmax = mls[i] \r\n\treturn max", "tests": "assert max_len_sub([2, 5, 6, 3, 7, 6, 5, 8], 8) == 5\nassert max_len_sub([-2, -1, 5, -1, 4, 0, 3], 7) == 4\nassert max_len_sub([9, 11, 13, 15, 18], 5) == 1", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/61", "original_task_id": 61, "entry_point": "count_Substrings", "prompt": "Write a python function to count number of substrings with the sum of digits equal to their length.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef count_Substrings(s, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to count number of substrings with the sum of digits equal to their length.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "from collections import defaultdict\r\ndef count_Substrings(s,n):\r\n    count,sum = 0,0\r\n    mp = defaultdict(lambda : 0)\r\n    mp[0] += 1\r\n    for i in range(n):\r\n        sum += ord(s[i]) - ord('0')\r\n        count += mp[sum - (i + 1)]\r\n        mp[sum - (i + 1)] += 1\r\n    return count", "tests": "assert count_Substrings('112112',6) == 6\nassert count_Substrings('111',3) == 6\nassert count_Substrings('1101112',7) == 12", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
