{"task_id": "Mbpp/78", "original_task_id": 78, "entry_point": "count_With_Odd_SetBits", "prompt": "Write a python function to find number of integers with odd number of set bits.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef count_With_Odd_SetBits(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find number of integers with odd number of set bits.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def count_With_Odd_SetBits(n): \r\n    if (n % 2 != 0): \r\n        return (n + 1) / 2\r\n    count = bin(n).count('1') \r\n    ans = n / 2\r\n    if (count % 2 != 0): \r\n        ans += 1\r\n    return ans ", "tests": "assert count_With_Odd_SetBits(5) == 3\nassert count_With_Odd_SetBits(10) == 5\nassert count_With_Odd_SetBits(15) == 8", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
