{"task_id": "Mbpp/80", "original_task_id": 80, "entry_point": "tetrahedral_number", "prompt": "Write a function to find the nth tetrahedral number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef tetrahedral_number(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the nth tetrahedral number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def tetrahedral_number(n): \r\n\treturn (n * (n + 1) * (n + 2)) / 6", "tests": "assert tetrahedral_number(5) == 35.0\nassert tetrahedral_number(6) == 56.0\nassert tetrahedral_number(7) == 84.0", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/81", "original_task_id": 81, "entry_point": "zip_tuples", "prompt": "Write a function to zip the two given tuples.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef zip_tuples(test_tup1, test_tup2):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to zip the two given tuples.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def zip_tuples(test_tup1, test_tup2):\r\n  res = []\r\n  for i, j in enumerate(test_tup1):\r\n    res.append((j, test_tup2[i % len(test_tup2)])) \r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert zip_tuples((7, 8, 4, 5, 9, 10),(1, 5, 6) ) == [(7, 1), (8, 5), (4, 6), (5, 1), (9, 5), (10, 6)]\nassert zip_tuples((8, 9, 5, 6, 10, 11),(2, 6, 7) ) == [(8, 2), (9, 6), (5, 7), (6, 2), (10, 6), (11, 7)]\nassert zip_tuples((9, 10, 6, 7, 11, 12),(3, 7, 8) ) == [(9, 3), (10, 7), (6, 8), (7, 3), (11, 7), (12, 8)]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
