{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "original_task_id": 92, "entry_point": "is_undulating", "prompt": "Write a function to check whether the given number is undulating or not.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef is_undulating(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to check whether the given number is undulating or not.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def is_undulating(n): \r\n\tif (len(n) <= 2): \r\n\t\treturn False\r\n\tfor i in range(2, len(n)): \r\n\t\tif (n[i - 2] != n[i]): \r\n\t\t\treturn False\r\n\treturn True", "tests": "assert is_undulating(\"1212121\") == True\nassert is_undulating(\"1991\") == False\nassert is_undulating(\"121\") == True", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/93", "original_task_id": 93, "entry_point": "power", "prompt": "Write a function to calculate the value of 'a' to the power 'b'.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef power(a, b):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to calculate the value of 'a' to the power 'b'.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def power(a,b):\r\n\tif b==0:\r\n\t\treturn 1\r\n\telif a==0:\r\n\t\treturn 0\r\n\telif b==1:\r\n\t\treturn a\r\n\telse:\r\n\t\treturn a*power(a,b-1)", "tests": "assert power(3,4) == 81\nassert power(2,3) == 8\nassert power(5,5) == 3125", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/94", "original_task_id": 94, "entry_point": "index_minimum", "prompt": "Write a function to extract the index minimum value record from the given tuples.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef index_minimum(test_list):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to extract the index minimum value record from the given tuples.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "from operator import itemgetter \r\ndef index_minimum(test_list):\r\n  res = min(test_list, key = itemgetter(1))[0]\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert index_minimum([('Rash', 143), ('Manjeet', 200), ('Varsha', 100)]) == 'Varsha'\nassert index_minimum([('Yash', 185), ('Dawood', 125), ('Sanya', 175)]) == 'Dawood'\nassert index_minimum([('Sai', 345), ('Salman', 145), ('Ayesha', 96)]) == 'Ayesha'", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
