{"task_id": "Mbpp/100", "original_task_id": 100, "entry_point": "next_smallest_palindrome", "prompt": "Write a function to find the next smallest palindrome of a specified number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef next_smallest_palindrome(num):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the next smallest palindrome of a specified number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import sys\r\ndef next_smallest_palindrome(num):\r\n    numstr = str(num)\r\n    for i in range(num+1,sys.maxsize):\r\n        if str(i) == str(i)[::-1]:\r\n            return i", "tests": "assert next_smallest_palindrome(99)==101\nassert next_smallest_palindrome(1221)==1331\nassert next_smallest_palindrome(120)==121", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/101", "original_task_id": 101, "entry_point": "kth_element", "prompt": "Write a function to find the kth element in the given array.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef kth_element(arr, n, k):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the kth element in the given array.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def kth_element(arr, n, k):\r\n  for i in range(n):\r\n    for j in range(0, n-i-1):\r\n      if arr[j] > arr[j+1]:\r\n        arr[j], arr[j+1] == arr[j+1], arr[j]\r\n  return arr[k-1]", "tests": "assert kth_element([12,3,5,7,19], 5, 2) == 3\nassert kth_element([17,24,8,23], 4, 3) == 8\nassert kth_element([16,21,25,36,4], 5, 4) == 36", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/102", "original_task_id": 102, "entry_point": "snake_to_camel", "prompt": "Write a function to convert snake case string to camel case string.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef snake_to_camel(word):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to convert snake case string to camel case string.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def snake_to_camel(word):\r\n        import re\r\n        return ''.join(x.capitalize() or '_' for x in word.split('_'))", "tests": "assert snake_to_camel('python_program')=='PythonProgram'\nassert snake_to_camel('python_language')==('PythonLanguage')\nassert snake_to_camel('programming_language')==('ProgrammingLanguage')", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "original_task_id": 103, "entry_point": "eulerian_num", "prompt": "Write a function to find eulerian number a(n, m).\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef eulerian_num(n, m):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find eulerian number a(n, m).", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def eulerian_num(n, m): \r\n\tif (m >= n or n == 0): \r\n\t\treturn 0 \r\n\tif (m == 0): \r\n\t\treturn 1 \r\n\treturn ((n - m) * eulerian_num(n - 1, m - 1) +(m + 1) * eulerian_num(n - 1, m))", "tests": "assert eulerian_num(3, 1) == 4\nassert eulerian_num(4, 1) == 11\nassert eulerian_num(5, 3) == 26", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/104", "original_task_id": 104, "entry_point": "sort_sublists", "prompt": "Write a function to sort each sublist of strings in a given list of lists using lambda function.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef sort_sublists(input_list):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to sort each sublist of strings in a given list of lists using lambda function.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def sort_sublists(input_list):\r\n    result = [sorted(x, key = lambda x:x[0]) for x in input_list] \r\n    return result\r", "tests": "assert sort_sublists(([\"green\", \"orange\"], [\"black\", \"white\"], [\"white\", \"black\", \"orange\"]))==[['green', 'orange'], ['black', 'white'], ['black', 'orange', 'white']]\nassert sort_sublists(([\" red \",\"green\" ],[\"blue \",\" black\"],[\" orange\",\"brown\"]))==[[' red ', 'green'], [' black', 'blue '], [' orange', 'brown']]\nassert sort_sublists(([\"zilver\",\"gold\"], [\"magnesium\",\"aluminium\"], [\"steel\", \"bronze\"]))==[['gold', 'zilver'],['aluminium', 'magnesium'], ['bronze', 'steel']]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
