{"task_id": "Mbpp/106", "original_task_id": 106, "entry_point": "add_lists", "prompt": "Write a function to add the given list to the given tuples.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef add_lists(test_list, test_tup):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to add the given list to the given tuples.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def add_lists(test_list, test_tup):\r\n  res = tuple(list(test_tup) + test_list)\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert add_lists([5, 6, 7], (9, 10)) == (9, 10, 5, 6, 7)\nassert add_lists([6, 7, 8], (10, 11)) == (10, 11, 6, 7, 8)\nassert add_lists([7, 8, 9], (11, 12)) == (11, 12, 7, 8, 9)", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/107", "original_task_id": 107, "entry_point": "count_Hexadecimal", "prompt": "Write a python function to count hexadecimal numbers for a given range.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef count_Hexadecimal(L, R):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to count hexadecimal numbers for a given range.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def count_Hexadecimal(L,R) :  \r\n    count = 0;  \r\n    for i in range(L,R + 1) : \r\n        if (i >= 10 and i <= 15) : \r\n            count += 1;  \r\n        elif (i > 15) : \r\n            k = i;  \r\n            while (k != 0) :  \r\n                if (k % 16 >= 10) : \r\n                    count += 1;  \r\n                k = k // 16;  \r\n    return count;  ", "tests": "assert count_Hexadecimal(10,15) == 6\nassert count_Hexadecimal(2,4) == 0\nassert count_Hexadecimal(15,16) == 1", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/108", "original_task_id": 108, "entry_point": "merge_sorted_list", "prompt": "Write a function to merge multiple sorted inputs into a single sorted iterator using heap queue algorithm.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef merge_sorted_list(num1, num2, num3):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to merge multiple sorted inputs into a single sorted iterator using heap queue algorithm.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import heapq\r\ndef merge_sorted_list(num1,num2,num3):\r\n  num1=sorted(num1)\r\n  num2=sorted(num2)\r\n  num3=sorted(num3)\r\n  result = heapq.merge(num1,num2,num3)\r\n  return list(result)", "tests": "assert merge_sorted_list([25, 24, 15, 4, 5, 29, 110],[19, 20, 11, 56, 25, 233, 154],[24, 26, 54, 48])==[4, 5, 11, 15, 19, 20, 24, 24, 25, 25, 26, 29, 48, 54, 56, 110, 154, 233]\nassert merge_sorted_list([1, 3, 5, 6, 8, 9], [2, 5, 7, 11], [1, 4, 7, 8, 12])==[1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 5, 6, 7, 7, 8, 8, 9, 11, 12]\nassert merge_sorted_list([18, 14, 10, 9, 8, 7, 9, 3, 2, 4, 1],[25, 35, 22, 85, 14, 65, 75, 25, 58],[12, 74, 9, 50, 61, 41])==[1, 2, 3, 4, 7, 8, 9, 9, 9, 10, 12, 14, 14, 18, 22, 25, 25, 35, 41, 50, 58, 61, 65, 74, 75, 85]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "original_task_id": 109, "entry_point": "odd_Equivalent", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the count of rotations of a binary string with odd value.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef odd_Equivalent(s, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the count of rotations of a binary string with odd value.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def odd_Equivalent(s,n): \r\n    count=0\r\n    for i in range(0,n): \r\n        if (s[i] == '1'): \r\n            count = count + 1\r\n    return count ", "tests": "assert odd_Equivalent(\"011001\",6) == 3\nassert odd_Equivalent(\"11011\",5) == 4\nassert odd_Equivalent(\"1010\",4) == 2", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/110", "original_task_id": 110, "entry_point": "extract_missing", "prompt": "Write a function to extract the ranges that are missing from the given list with the given start range and end range values.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef extract_missing(test_list, strt_val, stop_val):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to extract the ranges that are missing from the given list with the given start range and end range values.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def extract_missing(test_list, strt_val, stop_val):\r\n  res = []\r\n  for sub in test_list:\r\n    if sub[0] > strt_val:\r\n      res.append((strt_val, sub[0]))\r\n      strt_val = sub[1]\r\n    if strt_val < stop_val:\r\n      res.append((strt_val, stop_val))\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert extract_missing([(6, 9), (15, 34), (48, 70)], 2, 100) == [(2, 6), (9, 100), (9, 15), (34, 100), (34, 48), (70, 100)]\nassert extract_missing([(7, 2), (15, 19), (38, 50)], 5, 60) == [(5, 7), (2, 60), (2, 15), (19, 60), (19, 38), (50, 60)]\nassert extract_missing([(7, 2), (15, 19), (38, 50)], 1, 52) == [(1, 7), (2, 52), (2, 15), (19, 52), (19, 38), (50, 52)]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "original_task_id": 111, "entry_point": "common_in_nested_lists", "prompt": "Write a function to find common elements in given nested lists. * list item * list item * list item * list item\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef common_in_nested_lists(nestedlist):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find common elements in given nested lists. * list item * list item * list item * list item", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def common_in_nested_lists(nestedlist):\r\n    result = list(set.intersection(*map(set, nestedlist)))\r\n    return result", "tests": "assert common_in_nested_lists([[12, 18, 23, 25, 45], [7, 12, 18, 24, 28], [1, 5, 8, 12, 15, 16, 18]])==[18, 12]\nassert common_in_nested_lists([[12, 5, 23, 25, 45], [7, 11, 5, 23, 28], [1, 5, 8, 18, 23, 16]])==[5,23]\nassert common_in_nested_lists([[2, 3,4, 1], [4, 5], [6,4, 8],[4, 5], [6, 8,4]])==[4]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
