{"task_id": "Mbpp/113", "original_task_id": 113, "entry_point": "check_integer", "prompt": "Write a function to check if a string represents an integer or not.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef check_integer(text):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to check if a string represents an integer or not.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def check_integer(text):\r\n text = text.strip()\r\n if len(text) < 1:\r\n    return None\r\n else:\r\n     if all(text[i] in \"0123456789\" for i in range(len(text))):\r\n          return True\r\n     elif (text[0] in \"+-\") and \\\r\n         all(text[i] in \"0123456789\" for i in range(1,len(text))):\r\n         return True\r\n     else:\r\n        return False", "tests": "assert check_integer(\"python\")==False\nassert check_integer(\"1\")==True\nassert check_integer(\"12345\")==True", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/114", "original_task_id": 114, "entry_point": "assign_freq", "prompt": "Write a function to assign frequency to each tuple in the given tuple list.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef assign_freq(test_list):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to assign frequency to each tuple in the given tuple list.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "from collections import Counter \r\ndef assign_freq(test_list):\r\n  res = [(*key, val) for key, val in Counter(test_list).items()]\r\n  return (str(res)) ", "tests": "assert assign_freq([(6, 5, 8), (2, 7), (6, 5, 8), (6, 5, 8), (9, ), (2, 7)] ) == '[(6, 5, 8, 3), (2, 7, 2), (9, 1)]'\nassert assign_freq([(4, 2, 4), (7, 1), (4, 8), (4, 2, 4), (9, 2), (7, 1)] ) == '[(4, 2, 4, 2), (7, 1, 2), (4, 8, 1), (9, 2, 1)]'\nassert assign_freq([(11, 13, 10), (17, 21), (4, 2, 3), (17, 21), (9, 2), (4, 2, 3)] ) == '[(11, 13, 10, 1), (17, 21, 2), (4, 2, 3, 2), (9, 2, 1)]'", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
