{"task_id": "Mbpp/117", "original_task_id": 117, "entry_point": "list_to_float", "prompt": "Write a function to convert all possible convertible elements in the list to float.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef list_to_float(test_list):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to convert all possible convertible elements in the list to float.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def list_to_float(test_list):\r\n  res = []\r\n  for tup in test_list:\r\n    temp = []\r\n    for ele in tup:\r\n      if ele.isalpha():\r\n        temp.append(ele)\r\n      else:\r\n        temp.append(float(ele))\r\n    res.append((temp[0],temp[1])) \r\n  return (str(res)) ", "tests": "assert list_to_float( [(\"3\", \"4\"), (\"1\", \"26.45\"), (\"7.32\", \"8\"), (\"4\", \"8\")] ) == '[(3.0, 4.0), (1.0, 26.45), (7.32, 8.0), (4.0, 8.0)]'\nassert list_to_float( [(\"4\", \"4\"), (\"2\", \"27\"), (\"4.12\", \"9\"), (\"7\", \"11\")] ) == '[(4.0, 4.0), (2.0, 27.0), (4.12, 9.0), (7.0, 11.0)]'\nassert list_to_float( [(\"6\", \"78\"), (\"5\", \"26.45\"), (\"1.33\", \"4\"), (\"82\", \"13\")] ) == '[(6.0, 78.0), (5.0, 26.45), (1.33, 4.0), (82.0, 13.0)]'", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/118", "original_task_id": 118, "entry_point": "string_to_list", "prompt": "[link text](https:// [link text](https:// [link text](https://)))write a function to convert a string to a list.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef string_to_list(string):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "[link text](https:// [link text](https:// [link text](https://)))write a function to convert a string to a list.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def string_to_list(string): \r\n    lst = list(string.split(\" \")) \r\n    return lst", "tests": "assert string_to_list(\"python programming\")==['python','programming']\nassert string_to_list(\"lists tuples strings\")==['lists','tuples','strings']\nassert string_to_list(\"write a program\")==['write','a','program']", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/119", "original_task_id": 119, "entry_point": "search", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the element that appears only once in a sorted array.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef search(arr, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the element that appears only once in a sorted array.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def search(arr,n) :\r\n    XOR = 0\r\n    for i in range(n) :\r\n        XOR = XOR ^ arr[i]\r\n    return (XOR)", "tests": "assert search([1,1,2,2,3],5) == 3\nassert search([1,1,3,3,4,4,5,5,7,7,8],11) == 8\nassert search([1,2,2,3,3,4,4],7) == 1", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/120", "original_task_id": 120, "entry_point": "max_product_tuple", "prompt": "Write a function to find the maximum product from the pairs of tuples within a given list.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef max_product_tuple(list1):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the maximum product from the pairs of tuples within a given list.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def max_product_tuple(list1):\r\n    result_max = max([abs(x * y) for x, y in list1] )\r\n    return result_max", "tests": "assert max_product_tuple([(2, 7), (2, 6), (1, 8), (4, 9)] )==36\nassert max_product_tuple([(10,20), (15,2), (5,10)] )==200\nassert max_product_tuple([(11,44), (10,15), (20,5), (12, 9)] )==484", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/121", "original_task_id": 121, "entry_point": "check_triplet", "prompt": "Write a function to find the triplet with sum of the given array\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef check_triplet(A, n, sum, count):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the triplet with sum of the given array", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def check_triplet(A, n, sum, count):\r\n    if count == 3 and sum == 0:\r\n        return True\r\n    if count == 3 or n == 0 or sum < 0:\r\n        return False\r\n    return check_triplet(A, n - 1, sum - A[n - 1], count + 1) or\\\r\n           check_triplet(A, n - 1, sum, count)", "tests": "assert check_triplet([2, 7, 4, 0, 9, 5, 1, 3], 8, 6, 0) == True\nassert check_triplet([1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 5, 9], 8, 6, 0) == False\nassert check_triplet([10, 4, 2, 3, 5], 5, 15, 0) == True", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/122", "original_task_id": 122, "entry_point": "smartNumber", "prompt": "Write a function to find n’th smart number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef smartNumber(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find n’th smart number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "MAX = 3000 \r\ndef smartNumber(n): \r\n\tprimes = [0] * MAX \r\n\tresult = [] \r\n\tfor i in range(2, MAX): \r\n\t\tif (primes[i] == 0): \r\n\t\t\tprimes[i] = 1 \r\n\t\t\tj = i * 2 \r\n\t\t\twhile (j < MAX): \r\n\t\t\t\tprimes[j] -= 1 \r\n\t\t\t\tif ( (primes[j] + 3) == 0): \r\n\t\t\t\t\tresult.append(j) \r\n\t\t\t\tj = j + i \r\n\tresult.sort() \r\n\treturn result[n - 1] ", "tests": "assert smartNumber(1) == 30\nassert smartNumber(50) == 273\nassert smartNumber(1000) == 2664", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "original_task_id": 123, "entry_point": "amicable_numbers_sum", "prompt": "Write a function to sum all amicable numbers from 1 to a specified number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef amicable_numbers_sum(limit):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to sum all amicable numbers from 1 to a specified number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def amicable_numbers_sum(limit):\r\n    if not isinstance(limit, int):\r\n        return \"Input is not an integer!\"\r\n    if limit < 1:\r\n        return \"Input must be bigger than 0!\"\r\n    amicables = set()\r\n    for num in range(2, limit+1):\r\n        if num in amicables:\r\n            continue\r\n        sum_fact = sum([fact for fact in range(1, num) if num % fact == 0])\r\n        sum_fact2 = sum([fact for fact in range(1, sum_fact) if sum_fact % fact == 0])\r\n        if num == sum_fact2 and num != sum_fact:\r\n            amicables.add(num)\r\n            amicables.add(sum_fact2)\r\n    return sum(amicables)", "tests": "assert amicable_numbers_sum(999)==504\nassert amicable_numbers_sum(9999)==31626\nassert amicable_numbers_sum(99)==0", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/124", "original_task_id": 124, "entry_point": "angle_complex", "prompt": "Write a function to get the angle of a complex number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef angle_complex(a, b):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to get the angle of a complex number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import cmath\r\ndef angle_complex(a,b):\r\n  cn=complex(a,b)\r\n  angle=cmath.phase(a+b)\r\n  return angle", "tests": "assert angle_complex(0,1j)==1.5707963267948966 \nassert angle_complex(2,1j)==0.4636476090008061\nassert angle_complex(0,2j)==1.5707963267948966", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "original_task_id": 125, "entry_point": "find_length", "prompt": "Write a function to find the maximum difference between the number of 0s and number of 1s in any sub-string of the given binary string.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef find_length(string, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the maximum difference between the number of 0s and number of 1s in any sub-string of the given binary string.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def find_length(string, n): \r\n\tcurrent_sum = 0\r\n\tmax_sum = 0\r\n\tfor i in range(n): \r\n\t\tcurrent_sum += (1 if string[i] == '0' else -1) \r\n\t\tif current_sum < 0: \r\n\t\t\tcurrent_sum = 0\r\n\t\tmax_sum = max(current_sum, max_sum) \r\n\treturn max_sum if max_sum else 0", "tests": "assert find_length(\"11000010001\", 11) == 6\nassert find_length(\"10111\", 5) == 1\nassert find_length(\"11011101100101\", 14) == 2 ", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
