{"task_id": "Mbpp/136", "original_task_id": 136, "entry_point": "cal_electbill", "prompt": "Write a function to calculate electricity bill.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef cal_electbill(units):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to calculate electricity bill.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def cal_electbill(units):\r\n if(units < 50):\r\n    amount = units * 2.60\r\n    surcharge = 25\r\n elif(units <= 100):\r\n    amount = 130 + ((units - 50) * 3.25)\r\n    surcharge = 35\r\n elif(units <= 200):\r\n    amount = 130 + 162.50 + ((units - 100) * 5.26)\r\n    surcharge = 45\r\n else:\r\n    amount = 130 + 162.50 + 526 + ((units - 200) * 8.45)\r\n    surcharge = 75\r\n total = amount + surcharge\r\n return total", "tests": "assert cal_electbill(75)==246.25\nassert cal_electbill(265)==1442.75\nassert cal_electbill(100)==327.5", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "original_task_id": 137, "entry_point": "zero_count", "prompt": "Write a function to find the ration of zeroes in an array of integers.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef zero_count(nums):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the ration of zeroes in an array of integers.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "from array import array\r\ndef zero_count(nums):\r\n    n = len(nums)\r\n    n1 = 0\r\n    for x in nums:\r\n        if x == 0:\r\n            n1 += 1\r\n        else:\r\n          None\r\n    return round(n1/n,2)", "tests": "assert zero_count([0, 1, 2, -1, -5, 6, 0, -3, -2, 3, 4, 6, 8])==0.15\nassert zero_count([2, 1, 2, -1, -5, 6, 4, -3, -2, 3, 4, 6, 8])==0.00\nassert zero_count([2, 4, -6, -9, 11, -12, 14, -5, 17])==0.00", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "original_task_id": 138, "entry_point": "is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two", "prompt": "Write a python function to check whether the given number can be represented as sum of non-zero powers of 2 or not.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to check whether the given number can be represented as sum of non-zero powers of 2 or not.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(n): \r\n    if (n % 2 == 1): \r\n        return False\r\n    else: \r\n        return True", "tests": "assert is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(10) == True\nassert is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(7) == False\nassert is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(14) == True", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/139", "original_task_id": 139, "entry_point": "circle_circumference", "prompt": "Write a function to find the circumference of a circle.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef circle_circumference(r):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the circumference of a circle.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def circle_circumference(r):\r\n  perimeter=2*3.1415*r\r\n  return perimeter", "tests": "assert circle_circumference(10)==62.830000000000005\nassert circle_circumference(5)==31.415000000000003\nassert circle_circumference(4)==25.132", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/140", "original_task_id": 140, "entry_point": "extract_singly", "prompt": "Write a function to extract elements that occur singly in the given tuple list.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef extract_singly(test_list):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to extract elements that occur singly in the given tuple list.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def extract_singly(test_list):\r\n  res = []\r\n  temp = set()\r\n  for inner in test_list:\r\n    for ele in inner:\r\n      if not ele in temp:\r\n        temp.add(ele)\r\n        res.append(ele)\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert extract_singly([(3, 4, 5), (4, 5, 7), (1, 4)]) == [3, 4, 5, 7, 1]\nassert extract_singly([(1, 2, 3), (4, 2, 3), (7, 8)]) == [1, 2, 3, 4, 7, 8]\nassert extract_singly([(7, 8, 9), (10, 11, 12), (10, 11)]) == [7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "original_task_id": 141, "entry_point": "pancake_sort", "prompt": "Write a function to sort a list of elements using pancake sort.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef pancake_sort(nums):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to sort a list of elements using pancake sort.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def pancake_sort(nums):\r\n    arr_len = len(nums)\r\n    while arr_len > 1:\r\n        mi = nums.index(max(nums[0:arr_len]))\r\n        nums = nums[mi::-1] + nums[mi+1:len(nums)]\r\n        nums = nums[arr_len-1::-1] + nums[arr_len:len(nums)]\r\n        arr_len -= 1\r\n    return nums", "tests": "assert pancake_sort([15, 79, 25, 38, 69]) == [15, 25, 38, 69, 79]\nassert pancake_sort([98, 12, 54, 36, 85]) == [12, 36, 54, 85, 98]\nassert pancake_sort([41, 42, 32, 12, 23]) == [12, 23, 32, 41, 42]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/142", "original_task_id": 142, "entry_point": "count_samepair", "prompt": "Write a function to count the same pair in three given lists.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef count_samepair(list1, list2, list3):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to count the same pair in three given lists.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def count_samepair(list1,list2,list3):\r\n    result = sum(m == n == o for m, n, o in zip(list1,list2,list3))\r\n    return result", "tests": "assert count_samepair([1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8],[2,2,3,1,2,6,7,9],[2,1,3,1,2,6,7,9])==3\nassert count_samepair([1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8],[2,2,3,1,2,6,7,8],[2,1,3,1,2,6,7,8])==4\nassert count_samepair([1,2,3,4,2,6,7,8],[2,2,3,1,2,6,7,8],[2,1,3,1,2,6,7,8])==5", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/143", "original_task_id": 143, "entry_point": "find_lists", "prompt": "Write a function to find number of lists present in the given tuple.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef find_lists(Input):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find number of lists present in the given tuple.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def find_lists(Input): \r\n\tif isinstance(Input, list): \r\n\t\treturn 1\r\n\telse: \r\n\t\treturn len(Input) ", "tests": "assert find_lists(([1, 2, 3, 4], [5, 6, 7, 8])) == 2\nassert find_lists(([1, 2], [3, 4], [5, 6]))  == 3\nassert find_lists(([9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1])) == 1", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/144", "original_task_id": 144, "entry_point": "sum_Pairs", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the sum of absolute differences in all pairs of the given array.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef sum_Pairs(arr, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the sum of absolute differences in all pairs of the given array.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def sum_Pairs(arr,n): \r\n    sum = 0\r\n    for i in range(n - 1,-1,-1): \r\n        sum += i*arr[i] - (n-1-i) * arr[i] \r\n    return sum", "tests": "assert sum_Pairs([1,8,9,15,16],5) == 74\nassert sum_Pairs([1,2,3,4],4) == 10\nassert sum_Pairs([1,2,3,4,5,7,9,11,14],9) == 188", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/145", "original_task_id": 145, "entry_point": "max_Abs_Diff", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the maximum difference between any two elements in a given array.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef max_Abs_Diff(arr, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the maximum difference between any two elements in a given array.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def max_Abs_Diff(arr,n): \r\n    minEle = arr[0] \r\n    maxEle = arr[0] \r\n    for i in range(1, n): \r\n        minEle = min(minEle,arr[i]) \r\n        maxEle = max(maxEle,arr[i]) \r\n    return (maxEle - minEle) ", "tests": "assert max_Abs_Diff((2,1,5,3),4) == 4\nassert max_Abs_Diff((9,3,2,5,1),5) == 8\nassert max_Abs_Diff((3,2,1),3) == 2", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
