{"task_id": "Mbpp/172", "original_task_id": 172, "entry_point": "count_occurance", "prompt": "Write a function to find the occurence of characters 'std' in the given string 1. list item 1. list item 1. list item 2. list item 2. list item 2. list item\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef count_occurance(s):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the occurence of characters 'std' in the given string 1. list item 1. list item 1. list item 2. list item 2. list item 2. list item", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def count_occurance(s):\r\n  count=0\r\n  for i in range(len(s)):\r\n    if (s[i]== 's' and s[i+1]=='t' and s[i+2]== 'd'):\r\n      count = count + 1\r\n  return count", "tests": "assert count_occurance(\"letstdlenstdporstd\") == 3\nassert count_occurance(\"truststdsolensporsd\") == 1\nassert count_occurance(\"makestdsostdworthit\") == 2", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/173", "original_task_id": 173, "entry_point": "remove_splchar", "prompt": "Write a function to remove everything except alphanumeric characters from a string.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef remove_splchar(text):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to remove everything except alphanumeric characters from a string.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import re\r\ndef remove_splchar(text): \r\n pattern = re.compile('[\\W_]+')\r\n return (pattern.sub('', text))", "tests": "assert remove_splchar('python  @#&^%$*program123')==('pythonprogram123')\nassert remove_splchar('python %^$@!^&*()  programming24%$^^()    language')==('pythonprogramming24language')\nassert remove_splchar('python   ^%&^()(+_)(_^&67)                  program')==('python67program')", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/174", "original_task_id": 174, "entry_point": "group_keyvalue", "prompt": "Write a function to group a sequence of key-value pairs into a dictionary of lists.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef group_keyvalue(l):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to group a sequence of key-value pairs into a dictionary of lists.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def group_keyvalue(l):\r\n    result = {}\r\n    for k, v in l:\r\n         result.setdefault(k, []).append(v)\r\n    return result", "tests": "assert group_keyvalue([('yellow', 1), ('blue', 2), ('yellow', 3), ('blue', 4), ('red', 1)])=={'yellow': [1, 3], 'blue': [2, 4], 'red': [1]}\nassert group_keyvalue([('python', 1), ('python', 2), ('python', 3), ('python', 4), ('python', 5)])=={'python': [1,2,3,4,5]}\nassert group_keyvalue([('yellow',100), ('blue', 200), ('yellow', 300), ('blue', 400), ('red', 100)])=={'yellow': [100, 300], 'blue': [200, 400], 'red': [100]}", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/175", "original_task_id": 175, "entry_point": "is_valid_parenthese", "prompt": "Write a function to verify validity of a string of parentheses.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef is_valid_parenthese(str1):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to verify validity of a string of parentheses.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def is_valid_parenthese( str1):\r\n        stack, pchar = [], {\"(\": \")\", \"{\": \"}\", \"[\": \"]\"}\r\n        for parenthese in str1:\r\n            if parenthese in pchar:\r\n                stack.append(parenthese)\r\n            elif len(stack) == 0 or pchar[stack.pop()] != parenthese:\r\n                return False\r\n        return len(stack) == 0", "tests": "assert is_valid_parenthese(\"(){}[]\")==True\nassert is_valid_parenthese(\"()[{)}\")==False\nassert is_valid_parenthese(\"()\")==True", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
