{"task_id": "Mbpp/187", "original_task_id": 187, "entry_point": "longest_common_subsequence", "prompt": "Write a function to find the longest common subsequence for the given two sequences.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef longest_common_subsequence(X, Y, m, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the longest common subsequence for the given two sequences.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def longest_common_subsequence(X, Y, m, n): \r\n    if m == 0 or n == 0: \r\n       return 0 \r\n    elif X[m-1] == Y[n-1]: \r\n       return 1 + longest_common_subsequence(X, Y, m-1, n-1) \r\n    else: \r\n       return max(longest_common_subsequence(X, Y, m, n-1), longest_common_subsequence(X, Y, m-1, n))", "tests": "assert longest_common_subsequence(\"AGGTAB\" , \"GXTXAYB\", 6, 7) == 4\nassert longest_common_subsequence(\"ABCDGH\" , \"AEDFHR\", 6, 6) == 3\nassert longest_common_subsequence(\"AXYT\" , \"AYZX\", 4, 4) == 2", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/188", "original_task_id": 188, "entry_point": "prod_Square", "prompt": "Write a python function to check whether the given number can be represented by product of two squares or not.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef prod_Square(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to check whether the given number can be represented by product of two squares or not.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def prod_Square(n):\r\n    for i in range(2,(n) + 1):\r\n        if (i*i < (n+1)):\r\n            for j in range(2,n + 1):\r\n                if ((i*i*j*j) == n):\r\n                    return True;\r\n    return False;", "tests": "assert prod_Square(25) == False\nassert prod_Square(30) == False\nassert prod_Square(16) == True", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/189", "original_task_id": 189, "entry_point": "first_Missing_Positive", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the first missing positive number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef first_Missing_Positive(arr, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the first missing positive number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def first_Missing_Positive(arr,n): \r\n    ptr = 0\r\n    for i in range(n):\r\n        if arr[i] == 1:\r\n            ptr = 1\r\n            break\r\n    if ptr == 0:\r\n        return(1)\r\n    for i in range(n):\r\n        if arr[i] <= 0 or arr[i] > n:\r\n            arr[i] = 1\r\n    for i in range(n):\r\n        arr[(arr[i] - 1) % n] += n\r\n    for i in range(n):\r\n        if arr[i] <= n:\r\n            return(i + 1)\r\n    return(n + 1)", "tests": "assert first_Missing_Positive([1,2,3,-1,5],5) == 4\nassert first_Missing_Positive([0,-1,-2,1,5,8],6) == 2\nassert first_Missing_Positive([0,1,2,5,-8],5) == 3", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
