{"task_id": "Mbpp/194", "original_task_id": 194, "entry_point": "octal_To_Decimal", "prompt": "Write a python function to convert octal number to decimal number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef octal_To_Decimal(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to convert octal number to decimal number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def octal_To_Decimal(n):  \r\n    num = n; \r\n    dec_value = 0; \r\n    base = 1; \r\n    temp = num; \r\n    while (temp): \r\n        last_digit = temp % 10; \r\n        temp = int(temp / 10); \r\n        dec_value += last_digit*base; \r\n        base = base * 8; \r\n    return dec_value; ", "tests": "assert octal_To_Decimal(25) == 21\nassert octal_To_Decimal(30) == 24\nassert octal_To_Decimal(40) == 32", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/195", "original_task_id": 195, "entry_point": "first", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the first position of an element in a sorted array.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef first(arr, x, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the first position of an element in a sorted array.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def first(arr,x,n): \r\n    low = 0\r\n    high = n - 1\r\n    res = -1  \r\n    while (low <= high):\r\n        mid = (low + high) // 2 \r\n        if arr[mid] > x:\r\n            high = mid - 1\r\n        elif arr[mid] < x:\r\n            low = mid + 1\r\n        else:\r\n            res = mid\r\n            high = mid - 1\r\n    return res", "tests": "assert first([1,2,3,4,5,6,6],6,6) == 5\nassert first([1,2,2,2,3,2,2,4,2],2,9) == 1\nassert first([1,2,3],1,3) == 0", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
