{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "original_task_id": 235, "entry_point": "even_bit_set_number", "prompt": "Write a python function to set all even bits of a given number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef even_bit_set_number(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to set all even bits of a given number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def even_bit_set_number(n): \r\n    count = 0;res = 0;temp = n \r\n    while(temp > 0): \r\n        if (count % 2 == 1): \r\n            res |= (1 << count)\r\n        count+=1\r\n        temp >>= 1\r\n    return (n | res) ", "tests": "assert even_bit_set_number(10) == 10\nassert even_bit_set_number(20) == 30\nassert even_bit_set_number(30) == 30", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/236", "original_task_id": 236, "entry_point": "No_of_Triangle", "prompt": "Write a python function to count the maximum number of equilateral triangles that can be formed within a given equilateral triangle.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef No_of_Triangle(N, K):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to count the maximum number of equilateral triangles that can be formed within a given equilateral triangle.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def No_of_Triangle(N,K):\r\n    if (N < K):\r\n        return -1;\r\n    else:\r\n        Tri_up = 0;\r\n        Tri_up = ((N - K + 1) *(N - K + 2)) // 2;\r\n        Tri_down = 0;\r\n        Tri_down = ((N - 2 * K + 1) *(N - 2 * K + 2)) // 2;\r\n        return Tri_up + Tri_down;", "tests": "assert No_of_Triangle(4,2) == 7\nassert No_of_Triangle(4,3) == 3\nassert No_of_Triangle(1,3) == -1", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "original_task_id": 237, "entry_point": "check_occurences", "prompt": "Write a function to check the occurrences of records which occur similar times in the given tuples.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef check_occurences(test_list):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to check the occurrences of records which occur similar times in the given tuples.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "from collections import Counter \r\ndef check_occurences(test_list):\r\n  res = dict(Counter(tuple(ele) for ele in map(sorted, test_list)))\r\n  return  (res) ", "tests": "assert check_occurences([(3, 1), (1, 3), (2, 5), (5, 2), (6, 3)] ) == {(1, 3): 2, (2, 5): 2, (3, 6): 1}\nassert check_occurences([(4, 2), (2, 4), (3, 6), (6, 3), (7, 4)] ) == {(2, 4): 2, (3, 6): 2, (4, 7): 1}\nassert check_occurences([(13, 2), (11, 23), (12, 25), (25, 12), (16, 23)] ) == {(2, 13): 1, (11, 23): 1, (12, 25): 2, (16, 23): 1}", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
