{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "original_task_id": 239, "entry_point": "get_total_number_of_sequences", "prompt": "Write a function to find the number of possible sequences of length n such that each of the next element is greater than or equal to twice of the previous element but less than or equal to m.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef get_total_number_of_sequences(m, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the number of possible sequences of length n such that each of the next element is greater than or equal to twice of the previous element but less than or equal to m.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m,n): \r\n\tT=[[0 for i in range(n+1)] for i in range(m+1)] \r\n\tfor i in range(m+1): \r\n\t\tfor j in range(n+1): \r\n\t\t\tif i==0 or j==0: \r\n\t\t\t\tT[i][j]=0\r\n\t\t\telif i<j: \r\n\t\t\t\tT[i][j]=0\r\n\t\t\telif j==1: \r\n\t\t\t\tT[i][j]=i \r\n\t\t\telse: \r\n\t\t\t\tT[i][j]=T[i-1][j]+T[i//2][j-1] \r\n\treturn T[m][n]", "tests": "assert get_total_number_of_sequences(10, 4) == 4\nassert get_total_number_of_sequences(5, 2) == 6\nassert get_total_number_of_sequences(16, 3) == 84", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
