{"task_id": "Mbpp/270", "original_task_id": 270, "entry_point": "sum_even_and_even_index", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the sum of even numbers at even positions.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef sum_even_and_even_index(arr, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the sum of even numbers at even positions.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def sum_even_and_even_index(arr,n):  \r\n    i = 0\r\n    sum = 0\r\n    for i in range(0,n,2): \r\n        if (arr[i] % 2 == 0) : \r\n            sum += arr[i]  \r\n    return sum", "tests": "assert sum_even_and_even_index([5, 6, 12, 1, 18, 8],6) == 30\nassert sum_even_and_even_index([3, 20, 17, 9, 2, 10, 18, 13, 6, 18],10) == 26\nassert sum_even_and_even_index([5, 6, 12, 1],4) == 12", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/271", "original_task_id": 271, "entry_point": "even_Power_Sum", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the sum of fifth power of first n even natural numbers.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef even_Power_Sum(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the sum of fifth power of first n even natural numbers.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def even_Power_Sum(n): \r\n    sum = 0; \r\n    for i in range(1,n+1): \r\n        j = 2*i; \r\n        sum = sum + (j*j*j*j*j); \r\n    return sum; ", "tests": "assert even_Power_Sum(2) == 1056\nassert even_Power_Sum(3) == 8832\nassert even_Power_Sum(1) == 32", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/272", "original_task_id": 272, "entry_point": "rear_extract", "prompt": "Write a function to perfom the rear element extraction from list of tuples records.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef rear_extract(test_list):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to perfom the rear element extraction from list of tuples records.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def rear_extract(test_list):\r\n  res = [lis[-1] for lis in test_list]\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert rear_extract([(1, 'Rash', 21), (2, 'Varsha', 20), (3, 'Kil', 19)]) == [21, 20, 19]\nassert rear_extract([(1, 'Sai', 36), (2, 'Ayesha', 25), (3, 'Salman', 45)]) == [36, 25, 45]\nassert rear_extract([(1, 'Sudeep', 14), (2, 'Vandana', 36), (3, 'Dawood', 56)]) == [14, 36, 56]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/273", "original_task_id": 273, "entry_point": "substract_elements", "prompt": "Write a function to substract the contents of one tuple with corresponding index of other tuple.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef substract_elements(test_tup1, test_tup2):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to substract the contents of one tuple with corresponding index of other tuple.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def substract_elements(test_tup1, test_tup2):\r\n  res = tuple(map(lambda i, j: i - j, test_tup1, test_tup2))\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert substract_elements((10, 4, 5), (2, 5, 18)) == (8, -1, -13)\nassert substract_elements((11, 2, 3), (24, 45 ,16)) == (-13, -43, -13)\nassert substract_elements((7, 18, 9), (10, 11, 12)) == (-3, 7, -3)", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/274", "original_task_id": 274, "entry_point": "even_binomial_Coeff_Sum", "prompt": "Write a python function to find sum of even index binomial coefficients.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef even_binomial_Coeff_Sum(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find sum of even index binomial coefficients.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import math  \r\ndef even_binomial_Coeff_Sum( n): \r\n    return (1 << (n - 1)) ", "tests": "assert even_binomial_Coeff_Sum(4) == 8\nassert even_binomial_Coeff_Sum(6) == 32\nassert even_binomial_Coeff_Sum(2) == 2", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/275", "original_task_id": 275, "entry_point": "get_Position", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the position of the last removed element from the given array.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef get_Position(a, n, m):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the position of the last removed element from the given array.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import math as mt \r\ndef get_Position(a,n,m): \r\n    for i in range(n): \r\n        a[i] = (a[i] // m + (a[i] % m != 0))  \r\n    result,maxx = -1,-1\r\n    for i in range(n - 1,-1,-1): \r\n        if (maxx < a[i]): \r\n            maxx = a[i] \r\n            result = i \r\n    return result + 1", "tests": "assert get_Position([2,5,4],3,2) == 2\nassert get_Position([4,3],2,2) == 2\nassert get_Position([1,2,3,4],4,1) == 4", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
