{"task_id": "Mbpp/285", "original_task_id": 285, "entry_point": "text_match_two_three", "prompt": "Write a function that matches a string that has an a followed by two to three 'b'.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef text_match_two_three(text):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function that matches a string that has an a followed by two to three 'b'.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import re\r\ndef text_match_two_three(text):\r\n        patterns = 'ab{2,3}'\r\n        if re.search(patterns,  text):\r\n                return 'Found a match!'\r\n        else:\r\n                return('Not matched!')", "tests": "assert text_match_two_three(\"ac\")==('Not matched!')\nassert text_match_two_three(\"dc\")==('Not matched!')\nassert text_match_two_three(\"abbbba\")==('Found a match!')", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "original_task_id": 286, "entry_point": "max_sub_array_sum_repeated", "prompt": "Write a function to find the largest sum of contiguous array in the modified array which is formed by repeating the given array k times.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef max_sub_array_sum_repeated(a, n, k):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the largest sum of contiguous array in the modified array which is formed by repeating the given array k times.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(a, n, k): \r\n\tmax_so_far = -2147483648\r\n\tmax_ending_here = 0\r\n\tfor i in range(n*k): \r\n\t\tmax_ending_here = max_ending_here + a[i%n] \r\n\t\tif (max_so_far < max_ending_here): \r\n\t\t\tmax_so_far = max_ending_here \r\n\t\tif (max_ending_here < 0): \r\n\t\t\tmax_ending_here = 0\r\n\treturn max_so_far", "tests": "assert max_sub_array_sum_repeated([10, 20, -30, -1], 4, 3) == 30\nassert max_sub_array_sum_repeated([-1, 10, 20], 3, 2) == 59\nassert max_sub_array_sum_repeated([-1, -2, -3], 3, 3) == -1", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/287", "original_task_id": 287, "entry_point": "square_Sum", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the sum of squares of first n even natural numbers.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef square_Sum(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the sum of squares of first n even natural numbers.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def square_Sum(n):  \r\n    return int(2*n*(n+1)*(2*n+1)/3)", "tests": "assert square_Sum(2) == 20\nassert square_Sum(3) == 56\nassert square_Sum(4) == 120", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/288", "original_task_id": 288, "entry_point": "modular_inverse", "prompt": "Write a function to count array elements having modular inverse under given prime number p equal to itself.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef modular_inverse(arr, N, P):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to count array elements having modular inverse under given prime number p equal to itself.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def modular_inverse(arr, N, P):\r\n\tcurrent_element = 0\r\n\tfor i in range(0, N):\r\n\t\tif ((arr[i] * arr[i]) % P == 1):\r\n\t\t\tcurrent_element = current_element + 1\r\n\treturn current_element", "tests": "assert modular_inverse([ 1, 6, 4, 5 ], 4, 7) == 2\nassert modular_inverse([1, 3, 8, 12, 12], 5, 13) == 3\nassert modular_inverse([2, 3, 4, 5], 4, 6) == 1", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/289", "original_task_id": 289, "entry_point": "odd_Days", "prompt": "Write a python function to calculate the number of odd days in a given year.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef odd_Days(N):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to calculate the number of odd days in a given year.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def odd_Days(N): \r\n    hund1 = N // 100\r\n    hund4 = N // 400\r\n    leap = N >> 2\r\n    ordd = N - leap \r\n    if (hund1): \r\n        ordd += hund1 \r\n        leap -= hund1 \r\n    if (hund4): \r\n        ordd -= hund4 \r\n        leap += hund4 \r\n    days = ordd + leap * 2\r\n    odd = days % 7\r\n    return odd ", "tests": "assert odd_Days(100) == 5\nassert odd_Days(50) ==6\nassert odd_Days(75) == 2", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
