{"task_id": "Mbpp/322", "original_task_id": 322, "entry_point": "position_min", "prompt": "Write a function to find all index positions of the minimum values in a given list.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef position_min(list1):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find all index positions of the minimum values in a given list.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def position_min(list1):\r\n    min_val = min(list1)\r\n    min_result = [i for i, j in enumerate(list1) if j == min_val]\r\n    return min_result", "tests": "assert position_min([12,33,23,10,67,89,45,667,23,12,11,10,54])==[3,11]\nassert position_min([1,2,2,2,4,4,4,5,5,5,5])==[0]\nassert position_min([2,1,5,6,8,3,4,9,10,11,8,12])==[1]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/323", "original_task_id": 323, "entry_point": "re_arrange", "prompt": "Write a function to re-arrange the given array in alternating positive and negative items.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef re_arrange(arr, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to re-arrange the given array in alternating positive and negative items.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def right_rotate(arr, n, out_of_place, cur):\r\n\ttemp = arr[cur]\r\n\tfor i in range(cur, out_of_place, -1):\r\n\t\tarr[i] = arr[i - 1]\r\n\tarr[out_of_place] = temp\r\n\treturn arr\r\ndef re_arrange(arr, n):\r\n\tout_of_place = -1\r\n\tfor index in range(n):\r\n\t\tif (out_of_place >= 0):\r\n\t\t\tif ((arr[index] >= 0 and arr[out_of_place] < 0) or\r\n\t\t\t(arr[index] < 0 and arr[out_of_place] >= 0)):\r\n\t\t\t\tarr = right_rotate(arr, n, out_of_place, index)\r\n\t\t\t\tif (index-out_of_place > 2):\r\n\t\t\t\t\tout_of_place += 2\r\n\t\t\t\telse:\r\n\t\t\t\t\tout_of_place = - 1\r\n\t\tif (out_of_place == -1):\r\n\t\t\tif ((arr[index] >= 0 and index % 2 == 0) or\r\n\t\t\t (arr[index] < 0 and index % 2 == 1)):\r\n\t\t\t\tout_of_place = index\r\n\treturn arr", "tests": "assert re_arrange([-5, -2, 5, 2, 4,\t7, 1, 8, 0, -8], 10) == [-5, 5, -2, 2, -8, 4, 7, 1, 8, 0]\nassert re_arrange([1, 2, 3, -4, -1, 4], 6) == [-4, 1, -1, 2, 3, 4]\nassert re_arrange([4, 7, 9, 77, -4, 5, -3, -9], 8) == [-4, 4, -3, 7, -9, 9, 77, 5]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/324", "original_task_id": 324, "entry_point": "sum_of_alternates", "prompt": "Write a function to extract the sum of alternate chains of tuples.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef sum_of_alternates(test_tuple):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to extract the sum of alternate chains of tuples.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def sum_of_alternates(test_tuple):\r\n  sum1 = 0\r\n  sum2 = 0\r\n  for idx, ele in enumerate(test_tuple):\r\n    if idx % 2:\r\n      sum1 += ele\r\n    else:\r\n      sum2 += ele\r\n  return ((sum1),(sum2)) ", "tests": "assert sum_of_alternates((5, 6, 3, 6, 10, 34)) == (46, 18)\nassert sum_of_alternates((1, 2, 3, 4, 5)) == (6, 9)\nassert sum_of_alternates((6, 7, 8, 9, 4, 5)) == (21, 18)", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/325", "original_task_id": 325, "entry_point": "get_Min_Squares", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the minimum number of squares whose sum is equal to a given number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef get_Min_Squares(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the minimum number of squares whose sum is equal to a given number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def get_Min_Squares(n):\r\n    if n <= 3:\r\n        return n;\r\n    res = n \r\n    for x in range(1,n + 1):\r\n        temp = x * x;\r\n        if temp > n:\r\n            break\r\n        else:\r\n            res = min(res,1 + get_Min_Squares(n  - temp)) \r\n    return res;", "tests": "assert get_Min_Squares(6) == 3\nassert get_Min_Squares(2) == 2\nassert get_Min_Squares(4) == 1", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
