{"task_id": "Mbpp/342", "original_task_id": 342, "entry_point": "find_minimum_range", "prompt": "Write a function to find the smallest range that includes at-least one element from each of the given arrays.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef find_minimum_range(list):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the smallest range that includes at-least one element from each of the given arrays.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "from heapq import heappop, heappush\r\nclass Node:\r\n    def __init__(self, value, list_num, index):\r\n        self.value = value\r\n        self.list_num = list_num\r\n        self.index = index\r\n    def __lt__(self, other):\r\n        return self.value < other.value\r\ndef find_minimum_range(list):\r\n    high = float('-inf')\r\n    p = (0, float('inf'))\r\n    pq = []\r\n    for i in range(len(list)):\r\n        heappush(pq, Node(list[i][0], i, 0))\r\n        high = max(high, list[i][0])\r\n    while True:\r\n        top = heappop(pq)\r\n        low = top.value\r\n        i = top.list_num\r\n        j = top.index\r\n        if high - low < p[1] - p[0]:\r\n            p = (low, high)\r\n        if j == len(list[i]) - 1:\r\n            return p\r\n        heappush(pq, Node(list[i][j + 1], i, j + 1))\r\n        high = max(high, list[i][j + 1])", "tests": "assert find_minimum_range([[3, 6, 8, 10, 15], [1, 5, 12], [4, 8, 15, 16], [2, 6]]) == (4, 6)\nassert find_minimum_range([[ 2, 3, 4, 8, 10, 15 ], [1, 5, 12], [7, 8, 15, 16], [3, 6]]) == (4, 7)\nassert find_minimum_range([[4, 7, 9, 11, 16], [2, 6, 13], [5, 9, 16, 17], [3, 7]]) == (5, 7)", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/343", "original_task_id": 343, "entry_point": "dig_let", "prompt": "Write a function to calculate the number of digits and letters in a string.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef dig_let(s):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to calculate the number of digits and letters in a string.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def dig_let(s):\r\n d=l=0\r\n for c in s:\r\n    if c.isdigit():\r\n        d=d+1\r\n    elif c.isalpha():\r\n        l=l+1\r\n    else:\r\n        pass\r\n return (l,d)", "tests": "assert dig_let(\"python\")==(6,0)\nassert dig_let(\"program\")==(7,0)\nassert dig_let(\"python3.0\")==(6,2)", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
