{"task_id": "Mbpp/346", "original_task_id": 346, "entry_point": "zigzag", "prompt": "Write a function to find entringer number e(n, k).\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef zigzag(n, k):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find entringer number e(n, k).", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def zigzag(n, k): \r\n\tif (n == 0 and k == 0): \r\n\t\treturn 1\r\n\tif (k == 0): \r\n\t\treturn 0\r\n\treturn zigzag(n, k - 1) + zigzag(n - 1, n - k)", "tests": "assert zigzag(4, 3) == 5\nassert zigzag(4, 2) == 4\nassert zigzag(3, 1) == 1", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/347", "original_task_id": 347, "entry_point": "count_Squares", "prompt": "Write a python function to count the number of squares in a rectangle.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef count_Squares(m, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to count the number of squares in a rectangle.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def count_Squares(m,n): \r\n    if (n < m): \r\n        temp = m \r\n        m = n \r\n        n = temp \r\n    return n * (n + 1) * (3 * m - n + 1) // 6", "tests": "assert count_Squares(4,3) == 20\nassert count_Squares(1,2) == 2\nassert count_Squares(2,2) == 5", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/348", "original_task_id": 348, "entry_point": "find_ways", "prompt": "Write a function to count sequences of given length having non-negative prefix sums that can be generated by given values.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef find_ways(M):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to count sequences of given length having non-negative prefix sums that can be generated by given values.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def bin_coff(n, r): \r\n\tval = 1\r\n\tif (r > (n - r)): \r\n\t\tr = (n - r) \r\n\tfor i in range(0, r): \r\n\t\tval *= (n - i) \r\n\t\tval //= (i + 1) \r\n\treturn val \r\ndef find_ways(M): \r\n\tn = M // 2\r\n\ta = bin_coff(2 * n, n) \r\n\tb = a // (n + 1) \r\n\treturn (b) ", "tests": "assert find_ways(4) == 2\nassert find_ways(6) == 5\nassert find_ways(8) == 14", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/349", "original_task_id": 349, "entry_point": "check", "prompt": "Write a python function to check whether the given string is a binary string or not.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef check(string):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to check whether the given string is a binary string or not.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def check(string) :\r\n    p = set(string) \r\n    s = {'0', '1'} \r\n    if s == p or p == {'0'} or p == {'1'}: \r\n        return (\"Yes\") \r\n    else : \r\n        return (\"No\") ", "tests": "assert check(\"01010101010\") == \"Yes\"\nassert check(\"name0\") == \"No\"\nassert check(\"101\") == \"Yes\"", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/350", "original_task_id": 350, "entry_point": "minimum_Length", "prompt": "Write a python function to minimize the length of the string by removing occurrence of only one character.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef minimum_Length(s):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to minimize the length of the string by removing occurrence of only one character.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def minimum_Length(s) : \r\n    maxOcc = 0\r\n    n = len(s) \r\n    arr = [0]*26\r\n    for i in range(n) : \r\n        arr[ord(s[i]) -ord('a')] += 1\r\n    for i in range(26) : \r\n        if arr[i] > maxOcc : \r\n            maxOcc = arr[i] \r\n    return n - maxOcc ", "tests": "assert minimum_Length(\"mnm\") == 1\nassert minimum_Length(\"abcda\") == 3\nassert minimum_Length(\"abcb\") == 2", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/351", "original_task_id": 351, "entry_point": "first_Element", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the first element occurring k times in a given array.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef first_Element(arr, n, k):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the first element occurring k times in a given array.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def first_Element(arr,n,k): \r\n    count_map = {}; \r\n    for i in range(0, n): \r\n        if(arr[i] in count_map.keys()): \r\n            count_map[arr[i]] += 1\r\n        else: \r\n            count_map[arr[i]] = 1\r\n        i += 1\r\n    for i in range(0, n):  \r\n        if (count_map[arr[i]] == k): \r\n            return arr[i] \r\n        i += 1 \r\n    return -1", "tests": "assert first_Element([0,1,2,3,4,5],6,1) == 0\nassert first_Element([1,2,1,3,4],5,2) == 1\nassert first_Element([2,3,4,3,5,7,1,2,3,5],10,2) == 2", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
