{"task_id": "Mbpp/355", "original_task_id": 355, "entry_point": "count_Rectangles", "prompt": "Write a python function to count the number of rectangles in a circle of radius r.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef count_Rectangles(radius):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to count the number of rectangles in a circle of radius r.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def count_Rectangles(radius):  \r\n    rectangles = 0 \r\n    diameter = 2 * radius \r\n    diameterSquare = diameter * diameter \r\n    for a in range(1, 2 * radius):  \r\n        for b in range(1, 2 * radius): \r\n            diagnalLengthSquare = (a * a +  b * b)  \r\n            if (diagnalLengthSquare <= diameterSquare) : \r\n                rectangles += 1\r\n    return rectangles ", "tests": "assert count_Rectangles(2) == 8\nassert count_Rectangles(1) == 1\nassert count_Rectangles(0) == 0", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
