{"task_id": "Mbpp/399", "original_task_id": 399, "entry_point": "bitwise_xor", "prompt": "Write a function to perform the mathematical bitwise xor operation across the given tuples.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef bitwise_xor(test_tup1, test_tup2):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to perform the mathematical bitwise xor operation across the given tuples.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def bitwise_xor(test_tup1, test_tup2):\r\n  res = tuple(ele1 ^ ele2 for ele1, ele2 in zip(test_tup1, test_tup2))\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert bitwise_xor((10, 4, 6, 9), (5, 2, 3, 3)) == (15, 6, 5, 10)\nassert bitwise_xor((11, 5, 7, 10), (6, 3, 4, 4)) == (13, 6, 3, 14)\nassert bitwise_xor((12, 6, 8, 11), (7, 4, 5, 6)) == (11, 2, 13, 13)", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/400", "original_task_id": 400, "entry_point": "extract_freq", "prompt": "Write a function to extract the frequency of unique tuples in the given list order irrespective.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef extract_freq(test_list):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to extract the frequency of unique tuples in the given list order irrespective.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def extract_freq(test_list):\r\n  res = len(list(set(tuple(sorted(sub)) for sub in test_list)))\r\n  return (res)", "tests": "assert extract_freq([(3, 4), (1, 2), (4, 3), (5, 6)] ) == 3\nassert extract_freq([(4, 15), (2, 3), (5, 4), (6, 7)] ) == 4\nassert extract_freq([(5, 16), (2, 3), (6, 5), (6, 9)] ) == 4", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/401", "original_task_id": 401, "entry_point": "add_nested_tuples", "prompt": "Write a function to perform index wise addition of tuple elements in the given two nested tuples.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef add_nested_tuples(test_tup1, test_tup2):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to perform index wise addition of tuple elements in the given two nested tuples.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def add_nested_tuples(test_tup1, test_tup2):\r\n  res = tuple(tuple(a + b for a, b in zip(tup1, tup2))\r\n   for tup1, tup2 in zip(test_tup1, test_tup2))\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert add_nested_tuples(((1, 3), (4, 5), (2, 9), (1, 10)), ((6, 7), (3, 9), (1, 1), (7, 3))) == ((7, 10), (7, 14), (3, 10), (8, 13))\nassert add_nested_tuples(((2, 4), (5, 6), (3, 10), (2, 11)), ((7, 8), (4, 10), (2, 2), (8, 4))) == ((9, 12), (9, 16), (5, 12), (10, 15))\nassert add_nested_tuples(((3, 5), (6, 7), (4, 11), (3, 12)), ((8, 9), (5, 11), (3, 3), (9, 5))) == ((11, 14), (11, 18), (7, 14), (12, 17))", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/402", "original_task_id": 402, "entry_point": "ncr_modp", "prompt": "Write a function to compute the value of ncr%p.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef ncr_modp(n, r, p):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to compute the value of ncr%p.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def ncr_modp(n, r, p): \r\n    C = [0 for i in range(r+1)]   \r\n    C[0] = 1\r\n    for i in range(1, n+1): \r\n        for j in range(min(i, r), 0, -1): \r\n            C[j] = (C[j] + C[j-1]) % p   \r\n    return C[r] ", "tests": "assert ncr_modp(10,2,13)==6\nassert ncr_modp(15,12,43)==25\nassert ncr_modp(17,9,18)==10", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/403", "original_task_id": 403, "entry_point": "is_valid_URL", "prompt": "Write a function to check if a url is valid or not using regex.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef is_valid_URL(str):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to check if a url is valid or not using regex.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import re\r\ndef is_valid_URL(str):\r\n\tregex = (\"((http|https)://)(www.)?\" +\r\n\t\t\t\"[a-zA-Z0-9@:%._\\\\+~#?&//=]\" +\r\n\t\t\t\"{2,256}\\\\.[a-z]\" +\r\n\t\t\t\"{2,6}\\\\b([-a-zA-Z0-9@:%\" +\r\n\t\t\t\"._\\\\+~#?&//=]*)\")\r\n\tp = re.compile(regex)\r\n\tif (str == None):\r\n\t\treturn False\r\n\tif(re.search(p, str)):\r\n\t\treturn True\r\n\telse:\r\n\t\treturn False", "tests": "assert is_valid_URL(\"https://www.google.com\") == True\nassert is_valid_URL(\"https:/www.gmail.com\") == False\nassert is_valid_URL(\"https:// www.redit.com\") == False", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/404", "original_task_id": 404, "entry_point": "minimum", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the minimum of two numbers.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef minimum(a, b):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the minimum of two numbers.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def minimum(a,b):   \r\n    if a <= b: \r\n        return a \r\n    else: \r\n        return b ", "tests": "assert minimum(1,2) == 1\nassert minimum(-5,-4) == -5\nassert minimum(0,0) == 0", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/405", "original_task_id": 405, "entry_point": "check_tuplex", "prompt": "Write a function to check whether an element exists within a tuple.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef check_tuplex(tuplex, tuple1):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to check whether an element exists within a tuple.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def check_tuplex(tuplex,tuple1): \r\n  if tuple1 in tuplex:\r\n    return True\r\n  else:\r\n     return False", "tests": "assert check_tuplex((\"w\", 3, \"r\", \"e\", \"s\", \"o\", \"u\", \"r\", \"c\", \"e\"),'r')==True\nassert check_tuplex((\"w\", 3, \"r\", \"e\", \"s\", \"o\", \"u\", \"r\", \"c\", \"e\"),'5')==False\nassert check_tuplex((\"w\", 3, \"r\", \"e\", \"s\", \"o\", \"u\", \"r\", \"c\",\"e\"),3)==True", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/406", "original_task_id": 406, "entry_point": "find_Parity", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the parity of a given number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef find_Parity(x):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the parity of a given number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def find_Parity(x): \r\n    y = x ^ (x >> 1); \r\n    y = y ^ (y >> 2); \r\n    y = y ^ (y >> 4); \r\n    y = y ^ (y >> 8); \r\n    y = y ^ (y >> 16); \r\n    if (y & 1): \r\n        return (\"Odd Parity\"); \r\n    return (\"Even Parity\"); ", "tests": "assert find_Parity(12) == \"Even Parity\"\nassert find_Parity(7) == \"Odd Parity\"\nassert find_Parity(10) == \"Even Parity\"", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/407", "original_task_id": 407, "entry_point": "rearrange_bigger", "prompt": "Write a function to create the next bigger number by rearranging the digits of a given number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef rearrange_bigger(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to create the next bigger number by rearranging the digits of a given number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def rearrange_bigger(n):\r\n    nums = list(str(n))\r\n    for i in range(len(nums)-2,-1,-1):\r\n        if nums[i] < nums[i+1]:\r\n            z = nums[i:]\r\n            y = min(filter(lambda x: x > z[0], z))\r\n            z.remove(y)\r\n            z.sort()\r\n            nums[i:] = [y] + z\r\n            return int(\"\".join(nums))\r\n    return False", "tests": "assert rearrange_bigger(12)==21\nassert rearrange_bigger(10)==False\nassert rearrange_bigger(102)==120", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/408", "original_task_id": 408, "entry_point": "k_smallest_pairs", "prompt": "Write a function to find k number of pairs which consist of one element from the first array and one element from the second array.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef k_smallest_pairs(nums1, nums2, k):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find k number of pairs which consist of one element from the first array and one element from the second array.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import heapq\r\ndef k_smallest_pairs(nums1, nums2, k):\r\n   queue = []\r\n   def push(i, j):\r\n       if i < len(nums1) and j < len(nums2):\r\n           heapq.heappush(queue, [nums1[i] + nums2[j], i, j])\r\n   push(0, 0)\r\n   pairs = []\r\n   while queue and len(pairs) < k:\r\n       _, i, j = heapq.heappop(queue)\r\n       pairs.append([nums1[i], nums2[j]])\r\n       push(i, j + 1)\r\n       if j == 0:\r\n           push(i + 1, 0)\r\n   return pairs", "tests": "assert k_smallest_pairs([1,3,7],[2,4,6],2)==[[1, 2], [1, 4]]\nassert k_smallest_pairs([1,3,7],[2,4,6],1)==[[1, 2]]\nassert k_smallest_pairs([1,3,7],[2,4,6],7)==[[1, 2], [1, 4], [3, 2], [1, 6], [3, 4], [3, 6], [7, 2]]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/409", "original_task_id": 409, "entry_point": "min_product_tuple", "prompt": "Write a function to find the minimum product from the pairs of tuples within a given list.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef min_product_tuple(list1):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the minimum product from the pairs of tuples within a given list.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def min_product_tuple(list1):\r\n    result_min = min([abs(x * y) for x, y in list1] )\r\n    return result_min", "tests": "assert min_product_tuple([(2, 7), (2, 6), (1, 8), (4, 9)] )==8\nassert min_product_tuple([(10,20), (15,2), (5,10)] )==30\nassert min_product_tuple([(11,44), (10,15), (20,5), (12, 9)] )==100", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
