{"task_id": "Mbpp/478", "original_task_id": 478, "entry_point": "remove_lowercase", "prompt": "Write a function to remove lowercase substrings from a given string.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef remove_lowercase(str1):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to remove lowercase substrings from a given string.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import re\r\ndef remove_lowercase(str1):\r\n remove_lower = lambda text: re.sub('[a-z]', '', text)\r\n result =  remove_lower(str1)\r\n return result", "tests": "assert remove_lowercase(\"PYTHon\")==('PYTH')\nassert remove_lowercase(\"FInD\")==('FID')\nassert remove_lowercase(\"STRinG\")==('STRG')", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/479", "original_task_id": 479, "entry_point": "first_Digit", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the first digit of a given number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef first_Digit(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the first digit of a given number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def first_Digit(n) :  \r\n    while n >= 10:  \r\n        n = n / 10; \r\n    return int(n) ", "tests": "assert first_Digit(123) == 1\nassert first_Digit(456) == 4\nassert first_Digit(12) == 1", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/480", "original_task_id": 480, "entry_point": "get_max_occuring_char", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the maximum occurring character in a given string.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef get_max_occuring_char(str1):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the maximum occurring character in a given string.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def get_max_occuring_char(str1):\r\n  ASCII_SIZE = 256\r\n  ctr = [0] * ASCII_SIZE\r\n  max = -1\r\n  ch = ''\r\n  for i in str1:\r\n    ctr[ord(i)]+=1;\r\n  for i in str1:\r\n    if max < ctr[ord(i)]:\r\n      max = ctr[ord(i)]\r\n      ch = i\r\n  return ch", "tests": "assert get_max_occuring_char(\"data\") == \"a\"\nassert get_max_occuring_char(\"create\") == \"e\"\nassert get_max_occuring_char(\"brilliant girl\") == \"i\"", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/481", "original_task_id": 481, "entry_point": "is_subset_sum", "prompt": "Write a function to determine if there is a subset of the given set with sum equal to the given sum.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef is_subset_sum(set, n, sum):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to determine if there is a subset of the given set with sum equal to the given sum.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def is_subset_sum(set, n, sum):\r\n\tif (sum == 0):\r\n\t\treturn True\r\n\tif (n == 0):\r\n\t\treturn False\r\n\tif (set[n - 1] > sum):\r\n\t\treturn is_subset_sum(set, n - 1, sum)\r\n\treturn is_subset_sum(set, n-1, sum) or is_subset_sum(set, n-1, sum-set[n-1])", "tests": "assert is_subset_sum([3, 34, 4, 12, 5, 2], 6, 9) == True\nassert is_subset_sum([3, 34, 4, 12, 5, 2], 6, 30) == False\nassert is_subset_sum([3, 34, 4, 12, 5, 2], 6, 15) == True", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/482", "original_task_id": 482, "entry_point": "match", "prompt": "Write a function to find sequences of one upper case letter followed by lower case letters in the given string by using regex.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef match(text):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find sequences of one upper case letter followed by lower case letters in the given string by using regex.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import re \r\ndef match(text): \r\n\t\tpattern = '[A-Z]+[a-z]+$'\r\n\t\tif re.search(pattern, text): \r\n\t\t\t\treturn('Yes') \r\n\t\telse: \r\n\t\t\t\treturn('No') ", "tests": "assert match(\"Geeks\") == 'Yes'\nassert match(\"geeksforGeeks\") == 'Yes'\nassert match(\"geeks\") == 'No'", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/483", "original_task_id": 483, "entry_point": "first_Factorial_Divisible_Number", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the first natural number whose factorial is divisible by x.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef first_Factorial_Divisible_Number(x):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the first natural number whose factorial is divisible by x.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def first_Factorial_Divisible_Number(x): \r\n    i = 1;\r\n    fact = 1; \r\n    for i in range(1,x): \r\n        fact = fact * i \r\n        if (fact % x == 0): \r\n            break\r\n    return i ", "tests": "assert first_Factorial_Divisible_Number(10) == 5\nassert first_Factorial_Divisible_Number(15) == 5\nassert first_Factorial_Divisible_Number(5) == 4", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/484", "original_task_id": 484, "entry_point": "remove_matching_tuple", "prompt": "Write a function to remove the matching tuples from the given two tuples.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef remove_matching_tuple(test_list1, test_list2):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to remove the matching tuples from the given two tuples.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def remove_matching_tuple(test_list1, test_list2):\r\n  res = [sub for sub in test_list1 if sub not in test_list2]\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert remove_matching_tuple([('Hello', 'dude'), ('How', 'are'), ('you', '?')], [('Hello', 'dude'), ('How', 'are')]) == [('you', '?')]\nassert remove_matching_tuple([('Part', 'of'), ('the', 'journey'), ('is ', 'end')], [('Journey', 'the'), ('is', 'end')]) == [('Part', 'of'), ('the', 'journey'), ('is ', 'end')]\nassert remove_matching_tuple([('Its', 'been'), ('a', 'long'), ('day', 'without')], [('a', 'long'), ('my', 'friend')]) == [('Its', 'been'), ('day', 'without')]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/485", "original_task_id": 485, "entry_point": "largest_palindrome", "prompt": "Write a function to find the largest palindromic number in the given array.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef largest_palindrome(A, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the largest palindromic number in the given array.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def is_palindrome(n) : \r\n\tdivisor = 1\r\n\twhile (n / divisor >= 10) : \r\n\t\tdivisor *= 10\r\n\twhile (n != 0) : \r\n\t\tleading = n // divisor \r\n\t\ttrailing = n % 10\r\n\t\tif (leading != trailing) : \r\n\t\t\treturn False\r\n\t\tn = (n % divisor) // 10\r\n\t\tdivisor = divisor // 100\r\n\treturn True\r\ndef largest_palindrome(A, n) : \r\n\tA.sort() \r\n\tfor i in range(n - 1, -1, -1) : \r\n\t\tif (is_palindrome(A[i])) : \r\n\t\t\treturn A[i] \r\n\treturn -1", "tests": "assert largest_palindrome([1, 232, 54545, 999991], 4) == 54545\nassert largest_palindrome([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 50], 6) == 5\nassert largest_palindrome([1, 3, 7, 9, 45], 5)  == 9", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/486", "original_task_id": 486, "entry_point": "binomial_probability", "prompt": "Write a function to compute binomial probability for the given number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef binomial_probability(n, k, p):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to compute binomial probability for the given number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def nCr(n, r): \r\n\tif (r > n / 2): \r\n\t\tr = n - r \r\n\tanswer = 1 \r\n\tfor i in range(1, r + 1): \r\n\t\tanswer *= (n - r + i) \r\n\t\tanswer /= i \r\n\treturn answer \r\ndef binomial_probability(n, k, p): \r\n\treturn (nCr(n, k) * pow(p, k) *\tpow(1 - p, n - k)) ", "tests": "assert binomial_probability(10, 5, 1.0/3) == 0.13656454808718185\nassert binomial_probability(11, 6, 2.0/4) == 0.2255859375\nassert binomial_probability(12, 7, 3.0/5) == 0.227030335488", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/487", "original_task_id": 487, "entry_point": "sort_tuple", "prompt": "Write a function to sort a list of tuples in increasing order by the last element in each tuple.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef sort_tuple(tup):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to sort a list of tuples in increasing order by the last element in each tuple.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def sort_tuple(tup): \r\n\tlst = len(tup) \r\n\tfor i in range(0, lst): \r\n\t\tfor j in range(0, lst-i-1): \r\n\t\t\tif (tup[j][-1] > tup[j + 1][-1]): \r\n\t\t\t\ttemp = tup[j] \r\n\t\t\t\ttup[j]= tup[j + 1] \r\n\t\t\t\ttup[j + 1]= temp \r\n\treturn tup", "tests": "assert sort_tuple([(1, 3), (3, 2), (2, 1)] ) == [(2, 1), (3, 2), (1, 3)]\nassert sort_tuple([(2, 4), (3, 3), (1, 1)] ) == [(1, 1), (3, 3), (2, 4)]\nassert sort_tuple([(3, 9), (6, 7), (4, 3)] ) == [(4, 3), (6, 7), (3, 9)]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/488", "original_task_id": 488, "entry_point": "area_pentagon", "prompt": "Write a function to find the area of a pentagon.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef area_pentagon(a):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the area of a pentagon.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import math\r\ndef area_pentagon(a):\r\n  area=(math.sqrt(5*(5+2*math.sqrt(5)))*pow(a,2))/4.0\r\n  return area", "tests": "assert area_pentagon(5)==43.01193501472417\nassert area_pentagon(10)==172.0477400588967\nassert area_pentagon(15)==387.10741513251753", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/489", "original_task_id": 489, "entry_point": "frequency_Of_Largest", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the frequency of the largest value in a given array.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef frequency_Of_Largest(n, arr):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the frequency of the largest value in a given array.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def frequency_Of_Largest(n,arr): \r\n    mn = arr[0] \r\n    freq = 1\r\n    for i in range(1,n): \r\n        if (arr[i] >mn): \r\n            mn = arr[i] \r\n            freq = 1\r\n        elif (arr[i] == mn): \r\n            freq += 1\r\n    return freq ", "tests": "assert frequency_Of_Largest(5,[1,2,3,4,4]) == 2\nassert frequency_Of_Largest(3,[5,6,5]) == 1\nassert frequency_Of_Largest(4,[2,7,7,7]) == 3", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/490", "original_task_id": 490, "entry_point": "extract_symmetric", "prompt": "Write a function to extract all the pairs which are symmetric in the given tuple list.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef extract_symmetric(test_list):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to extract all the pairs which are symmetric in the given tuple list.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def extract_symmetric(test_list):\r\n  temp = set(test_list) & {(b, a) for a, b in test_list}\r\n  res = {(a, b) for a, b in temp if a < b}\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert extract_symmetric([(6, 7), (2, 3), (7, 6), (9, 8), (10, 2), (8, 9)] ) == {(8, 9), (6, 7)}\nassert extract_symmetric([(7, 8), (3, 4), (8, 7), (10, 9), (11, 3), (9, 10)] ) == {(9, 10), (7, 8)}\nassert extract_symmetric([(8, 9), (4, 5), (9, 8), (11, 10), (12, 4), (10, 11)] ) == {(8, 9), (10, 11)}", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/491", "original_task_id": 491, "entry_point": "sum_gp", "prompt": "Write a function to find the sum of geometric progression series.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef sum_gp(a, n, r):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the sum of geometric progression series.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import math\r\ndef sum_gp(a,n,r):\r\n total = (a * (1 - math.pow(r, n ))) / (1- r)\r\n return total", "tests": "assert sum_gp(1,5,2)==31\nassert sum_gp(1,5,4)==341\nassert sum_gp(2,6,3)==728", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "eval", "original_split": "test", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
