{"task_id": "Mbpp/971", "split": "train", "source_fields": {"task_id": 971, "text": "Write a function to find the maximum number of segments of lengths a, b and c that can be formed from n.", "code": "def maximum_segments(n, a, b, c) : \r\n\tdp = [-1] * (n + 10) \r\n\tdp[0] = 0\r\n\tfor i in range(0, n) : \r\n\t\tif (dp[i] != -1) : \r\n\t\t\tif(i + a <= n ): \r\n\t\t\t\tdp[i + a] = max(dp[i] + 1, \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdp[i + a]) \r\n\t\t\tif(i + b <= n ): \r\n\t\t\t\tdp[i + b] = max(dp[i] + 1, \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdp[i + b]) \r\n\t\t\tif(i + c <= n ): \r\n\t\t\t\tdp[i + c] = max(dp[i] + 1, \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdp[i + c]) \r\n\treturn dp[n]", "test_list": ["assert maximum_segments(7, 5, 2, 5) == 2", "assert maximum_segments(17, 2, 1, 3) == 17", "assert maximum_segments(18, 16, 3, 6) == 6"], "test_setup_code": "", "challenge_test_list": []}}
