{"task_id": "Mbpp/755", "split": "train", "source_fields": {"task_id": 755, "text": "Write a function to find the second smallest number in a list.", "code": "def second_smallest(numbers):\r\n  if (len(numbers)<2):\r\n    return\r\n  if ((len(numbers)==2)  and (numbers[0] == numbers[1]) ):\r\n    return\r\n  dup_items = set()\r\n  uniq_items = []\r\n  for x in numbers:\r\n    if x not in dup_items:\r\n      uniq_items.append(x)\r\n      dup_items.add(x)\r\n  uniq_items.sort()    \r\n  return  uniq_items[1] ", "test_list": ["assert second_smallest([1, 2, -8, -2, 0, -2])==-2", "assert second_smallest([1, 1, -0.5, 0, 2, -2, -2])==-0.5", "assert second_smallest([2,2])==None"], "test_setup_code": "", "challenge_test_list": []}}
