{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "split": "train", "source_fields": {"task_id": 630, "text": "Write a function to extract all the adjacent coordinates of the given coordinate tuple.", "code": "def adjac(ele, sub = []): \r\n  if not ele: \r\n     yield sub \r\n  else: \r\n     yield from [idx for j in range(ele[0] - 1, ele[0] + 2) \r\n                for idx in adjac(ele[1:], sub + [j])] \r\ndef get_coordinates(test_tup):\r\n  res = list(adjac(test_tup))\r\n  return (res) ", "test_list": ["assert get_coordinates((3, 4)) == [[2, 3], [2, 4], [2, 5], [3, 3], [3, 4], [3, 5], [4, 3], [4, 4], [4, 5]]", "assert get_coordinates((4, 5)) ==[[3, 4], [3, 5], [3, 6], [4, 4], [4, 5], [4, 6], [5, 4], [5, 5], [5, 6]]", "assert get_coordinates((5, 6)) == [[4, 5], [4, 6], [4, 7], [5, 5], [5, 6], [5, 7], [6, 5], [6, 6], [6, 7]]"], "test_setup_code": "", "challenge_test_list": []}}
