{"task_id": "Mbpp/355", "split": "eval", "source_fields": {"task_id": 355, "text": "Write a python function to count the number of rectangles in a circle of radius r.", "code": "def count_Rectangles(radius):  \r\n    rectangles = 0 \r\n    diameter = 2 * radius \r\n    diameterSquare = diameter * diameter \r\n    for a in range(1, 2 * radius):  \r\n        for b in range(1, 2 * radius): \r\n            diagnalLengthSquare = (a * a +  b * b)  \r\n            if (diagnalLengthSquare <= diameterSquare) : \r\n                rectangles += 1\r\n    return rectangles ", "test_list": ["assert count_Rectangles(2) == 8", "assert count_Rectangles(1) == 1", "assert count_Rectangles(0) == 0"], "test_setup_code": "", "challenge_test_list": []}}
