{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "original_task_id": 622, "entry_point": "get_median", "prompt": "Write a function to find the median of two sorted arrays of same size.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef get_median(arr1, arr2, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the median of two sorted arrays of same size.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def get_median(arr1, arr2, n):\r\n  i = 0\r\n  j = 0\r\n  m1 = -1\r\n  m2 = -1\r\n  count = 0\r\n  while count < n + 1:\r\n    count += 1\r\n    if i == n:\r\n      m1 = m2\r\n      m2 = arr2[0]\r\n      break\r\n    elif j == n:\r\n      m1 = m2\r\n      m2 = arr1[0]\r\n      break\r\n    if arr1[i] <= arr2[j]:\r\n      m1 = m2\r\n      m2 = arr1[i]\r\n      i += 1\r\n    else:\r\n      m1 = m2\r\n      m2 = arr2[j]\r\n      j += 1\r\n  return (m1 + m2)/2", "tests": "assert get_median([1, 12, 15, 26, 38], [2, 13, 17, 30, 45], 5) == 16.0\nassert get_median([2, 4, 8, 9], [7, 13, 19, 28], 4) == 8.5\nassert get_median([3, 6, 14, 23, 36, 42], [2, 18, 27, 39, 49, 55], 6) == 25.0", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/748", "original_task_id": 748, "entry_point": "capital_words_spaces", "prompt": "Write a function to put spaces between words starting with capital letters in a given string by using regex.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef capital_words_spaces(str1):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to put spaces between words starting with capital letters in a given string by using regex.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import re\r\ndef capital_words_spaces(str1):\r\n  return re.sub(r\"(\\w)([A-Z])\", r\"\\1 \\2\", str1)", "tests": "assert capital_words_spaces(\"Python\") == 'Python'\nassert capital_words_spaces(\"PythonProgrammingExamples\") == 'Python Programming Examples'\nassert capital_words_spaces(\"GetReadyToBeCodingFreak\") == 'Get Ready To Be Coding Freak'", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/811", "original_task_id": 811, "entry_point": "check_identical", "prompt": "Write a function to check if two lists of tuples are identical or not.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef check_identical(test_list1, test_list2):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to check if two lists of tuples are identical or not.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def check_identical(test_list1, test_list2):\r\n  res = test_list1 == test_list2\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert check_identical([(10, 4), (2, 5)], [(10, 4), (2, 5)]) == True\nassert check_identical([(1, 2), (3, 7)], [(12, 14), (12, 45)]) == False\nassert check_identical([(2, 14), (12, 25)], [(2, 14), (12, 25)]) == True", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/616", "original_task_id": 616, "entry_point": "tuple_modulo", "prompt": "Write a function to perfom the modulo of tuple elements in the given two tuples.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef tuple_modulo(test_tup1, test_tup2):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to perfom the modulo of tuple elements in the given two tuples.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def tuple_modulo(test_tup1, test_tup2):\r\n  res = tuple(ele1 % ele2 for ele1, ele2 in zip(test_tup1, test_tup2)) \r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert tuple_modulo((10, 4, 5, 6), (5, 6, 7, 5)) == (0, 4, 5, 1)\nassert tuple_modulo((11, 5, 6, 7), (6, 7, 8, 6)) == (5, 5, 6, 1)\nassert tuple_modulo((12, 6, 7, 8), (7, 8, 9, 7)) == (5, 6, 7, 1)", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/663", "original_task_id": 663, "entry_point": "find_max_val", "prompt": "Write a function to find the largest possible value of k such that k modulo x is y.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef find_max_val(n, x, y):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the largest possible value of k such that k modulo x is y.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import sys \r\ndef find_max_val(n, x, y): \r\n\tans = -sys.maxsize \r\n\tfor k in range(n + 1): \r\n\t\tif (k % x == y): \r\n\t\t\tans = max(ans, k) \r\n\treturn (ans if (ans >= 0 and\r\n\t\t\t\t\tans <= n) else -1) ", "tests": "assert find_max_val(15, 10, 5) == 15\nassert find_max_val(187, 10, 5) == 185\nassert find_max_val(16, 11, 1) == 12", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/860", "original_task_id": 860, "entry_point": "check_alphanumeric", "prompt": "Write a function to check whether the given string is ending with only alphanumeric characters or not using regex.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef check_alphanumeric(string):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to check whether the given string is ending with only alphanumeric characters or not using regex.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import re \r\nregex = '[a-zA-z0-9]$'\r\ndef check_alphanumeric(string): \r\n\tif(re.search(regex, string)): \r\n\t\treturn (\"Accept\") \r\n\telse: \r\n\t\treturn (\"Discard\") ", "tests": "assert check_alphanumeric(\"dawood@\") == 'Discard'\nassert check_alphanumeric(\"skdmsam326\") == 'Accept'\nassert check_alphanumeric(\"cooltricks@\") == 'Discard'", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/694", "original_task_id": 694, "entry_point": "extract_unique", "prompt": "Write a function to extract unique values from the given dictionary values.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef extract_unique(test_dict):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to extract unique values from the given dictionary values.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def extract_unique(test_dict):\r\n  res = list(sorted({ele for val in test_dict.values() for ele in val}))\r\n  return res", "tests": "assert extract_unique({'msm' : [5, 6, 7, 8],'is' : [10, 11, 7, 5],'best' : [6, 12, 10, 8],'for' : [1, 2, 5]} ) == [1, 2, 5, 6, 7, 8, 10, 11, 12]\nassert extract_unique({'Built' : [7, 1, 9, 4],'for' : [11, 21, 36, 14, 9],'ISP' : [4, 1, 21, 39, 47],'TV' : [1, 32, 38]} ) == [1, 4, 7, 9, 11, 14, 21, 32, 36, 38, 39, 47]\nassert extract_unique({'F' : [11, 13, 14, 17],'A' : [12, 11, 15, 18],'N' : [19, 21, 15, 36],'G' : [37, 36, 35]}) == [11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 17, 18, 19, 21, 35, 36, 37]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/834", "original_task_id": 834, "entry_point": "generate_matrix", "prompt": "Write a function to generate a square matrix filled with elements from 1 to n raised to the power of 2 in spiral order.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef generate_matrix(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to generate a square matrix filled with elements from 1 to n raised to the power of 2 in spiral order.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def generate_matrix(n):\r\n        if n<=0:\r\n            return [] \r\n        matrix=[row[:] for row in [[0]*n]*n]        \r\n        row_st=0\r\n        row_ed=n-1        \r\n        col_st=0\r\n        col_ed=n-1\r\n        current=1        \r\n        while (True):\r\n            if current>n*n:\r\n                break\r\n            for c in range (col_st, col_ed+1):\r\n                matrix[row_st][c]=current\r\n                current+=1\r\n            row_st+=1\r\n            for r in range (row_st, row_ed+1):\r\n                matrix[r][col_ed]=current\r\n                current+=1\r\n            col_ed-=1\r\n            for c in range (col_ed, col_st-1, -1):\r\n                matrix[row_ed][c]=current\r\n                current+=1\r\n            row_ed-=1\r\n            for r in range (row_ed, row_st-1, -1):\r\n                matrix[r][col_st]=current\r\n                current+=1\r\n            col_st+=1\r\n        return matrix", "tests": "assert generate_matrix(3)==[[1, 2, 3], [8, 9, 4], [7, 6, 5]] \nassert generate_matrix(2)==[[1,2],[4,3]]\nassert generate_matrix(7)==[[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7], [24, 25, 26, 27, 28, 29, 8], [23, 40, 41, 42, 43, 30, 9], [22, 39, 48, 49, 44, 31, 10], [21, 38, 47, 46, 45, 32, 11], [20, 37, 36, 35, 34, 33, 12], [19, 18, 17, 16, 15, 14, 13]]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/606", "original_task_id": 606, "entry_point": "radian_degree", "prompt": "Write a function to convert degrees to radians.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef radian_degree(degree):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to convert degrees to radians.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import math\r\ndef radian_degree(degree):\r\n radian = degree*(math.pi/180)\r\n return radian", "tests": "assert radian_degree(90)==1.5707963267948966\nassert radian_degree(60)==1.0471975511965976\nassert radian_degree(120)==2.0943951023931953", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
