{"task_id": "Mbpp/841", "original_task_id": 841, "entry_point": "get_inv_count", "prompt": "Write a function to count the number of inversions in the given array.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef get_inv_count(arr, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to count the number of inversions in the given array.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def get_inv_count(arr, n): \r\n\tinv_count = 0\r\n\tfor i in range(n): \r\n\t\tfor j in range(i + 1, n): \r\n\t\t\tif (arr[i] > arr[j]): \r\n\t\t\t\tinv_count += 1\r\n\treturn inv_count ", "tests": "assert get_inv_count([1, 20, 6, 4, 5], 5) == 5\nassert get_inv_count([8, 4, 2, 1], 4) == 6\nassert get_inv_count([3, 1, 2], 3) == 2", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
