{"task_id": "Mbpp/700", "original_task_id": 700, "entry_point": "count_range_in_list", "prompt": "Write a function to count the number of elements in a list which are within a specific range.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef count_range_in_list(li, min, max):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to count the number of elements in a list which are within a specific range.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def count_range_in_list(li, min, max):\r\n\tctr = 0\r\n\tfor x in li:\r\n\t\tif min <= x <= max:\r\n\t\t\tctr += 1\r\n\treturn ctr", "tests": "assert count_range_in_list([10,20,30,40,40,40,70,80,99],40,100)==6\nassert count_range_in_list(['a','b','c','d','e','f'],'a','e')==5\nassert count_range_in_list([7,8,9,15,17,19,45],15,20)==3", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/899", "original_task_id": 899, "entry_point": "check", "prompt": "Write a python function to check whether an array can be sorted or not by picking only the corner elements.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef check(arr, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to check whether an array can be sorted or not by picking only the corner elements.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def check(arr,n): \r\n    g = 0 \r\n    for i in range(1,n): \r\n        if (arr[i] - arr[i - 1] > 0 and g == 1): \r\n            return False\r\n        if (arr[i] - arr[i] < 0): \r\n            g = 1\r\n    return True", "tests": "assert check([3,2,1,2,3,4],6) == True\nassert check([2,1,4,5,1],5) == True\nassert check([1,2,2,1,2,3],6) == True", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
